{"timestamp": "2026-10-05T20:25:28.026042+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-254004db-5bd5-4022-9816-b8dc0dacf139', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You prepare the educational structure of one approved lesson.\\n\\nThe path owns the objective and concept identity. The skeleton supplies a strong\\nrecommended sequence and a closed legal slot catalogue. You may select the exact\\npedagogical sequence for this objective, but code validates the result.\\nA later planner will choose page blocks. You must not choose components, page\\nobjects, layouts, or question text.\\n\\n## FIXED INPUT\\n\\n- objective and objective_hash\\n- concept_id\\n- primary_knowledge_type\\n- lesson_mode\\n- recommended_slots and legal_slots with slot purposes\\n- hard_constraints including max_slots and verification\\n- scope_contract\\n- prior_established\\n- explicit prerequisites\\n- lesson_actuals\\n- carried anchor, when present\\n- resource identity and purpose\\n\\n## YOUR DECISIONS\\n\\n1. Draft zero to three real misconceptions. Each must support a confident wrong\\n   answer. A missing term is a knowledge gap, not a misconception.\\n2. Reuse the carried anchor when it fits. Otherwise choose one concrete anchor\\n   and state why it is new.\\n3. Choose selected_slots from legal_slots. Keep the recommendation when it fits;\\n   every meaningful departure needs flow_rationale and flow_departures.\\n4. Give each selected section a concise title and transition note. Return exactly\\n   one semantic section payload per selected slot, in selected order.\\n   The first section\\'s transition_note must be null; only later sections\\n   may explain how they follow the preceding section.\\n4. Do not output technical identity. The backend attaches objective, concept id,\\n   section id/role, and card_id after your response.\\n\\n## PROHIBITIONS\\n\\n- Never output or rewrite the objective or concept ID.\\n- Never invent a slot role, exceed max_slots, or remove the final\\n  verification/check capability.\\n- Never choose a component, page object, pedagogical block intent, placement,\\n  or visual form.\\n- Never write question text.\\n- Never reteach prior_established in the structural rationale.\\n- Never introduce must_not_introduce content.\\n- Never manufacture a misconception to fill a count.\\n- Never choose page blocks, intents, objects, or briefs. A later planner\\n  owns the teaching design.\\n\\nIf the objective cannot honestly fit the legal slot catalogue, emit deviation_request.\\nIf the objective itself is wrong, emit objective_concern. Do not repair either.\\n\\n## OUTPUT\\n\\nJSON only, matching the supplied output schema.\\n\\nThe output contains only:\\n\\n- anchor as {\"description\": str, \"source\": \"carried\"|\"new\"}\\n- one semantic concept-card payload (title/prereqs/misconceptions/opens_by;\\n  no id or objective)\\n- selected_slots, flow_rationale, and flow_departures\\n- sections with title and transition_note only, one per selected slot in order\\n- deviation_request or null\\n- objective_concern or null\\n\\nIt contains no components and no blocks.\\n\\n## SELF-CHECK\\n\\n1. Did I avoid outputting upstream-owned identity/objective fields?\\n2. Are selected_slots legal, bounded, and verification-complete?\\n3. Did I return exactly one section payload per selected slot, in order?\\n4. Does every misconception pass the confident-wrong-answer test?\\n5. Did I choose any page form or teaching block? Remove it.\\n6. Did I contradict prior_established, terminology, or exclusions?\\n'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"$defs\": {\"FlowDeparture\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"operation\": {\"enum\": [\"insert\", \"remove\", \"replace\", \"reorder\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"from_slot\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"to_slot\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"reason\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"operation\", \"reason\"], \"title\": \"FlowDeparture\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathAnchor\": {\"properties\": {\"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"source\": {\"enum\": [\"carried\", \"new\"], \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"description\", \"source\"], \"title\": \"PathAnchor\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathDeviationRequest\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"operation\": {\"enum\": [\"insert\", \"remove\", \"replace\", \"reorder\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"target_slot\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"replacement_slot\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}]}, \"reason\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"operation\", \"target_slot\", \"replacement_slot\", \"reason\"], \"title\": \"PathDeviationRequest\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathStructuralMisconception\": {\"properties\": {\"id\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"description\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"description\": \"The wrong belief, stated the way a learner would state it.\"}, \"statement\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"source\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"title\": \"PathStructuralMisconception\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathStructuralPageCard\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"title\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"prereqs\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"misconceptions\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathStructuralMisconception\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"no_known_misconceptions\": {\"default\": false, \"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"opens_by\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"title\": \"PathStructuralPageCard\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathStructuralPageSection\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"title\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"transition_note\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"title\"], \"title\": \"PathStructuralPageSection\", \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"anchor\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathAnchor\"}, \"cards\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathStructuralPageCard\"}, \"maxItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"sections\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathStructuralPageSection\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"selected_slots\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"flow_rationale\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"flow_departures\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FlowDeparture\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"deviation_request\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathDeviationRequest\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"objective_concern\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"anchor\"], \"title\": \"PathStructuralPagePlan\", \"type\": \"object\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{\\n  \"concept_id\": \"9704c8b6-3b96-49d1-ade2-ad4c55329be1\",\\n  \"exclusions\": [],\\n  \"external_prerequisites\": [],\\n  \"group_ids\": [],\\n  \"groups\": [],\\n  \"hard_constraints\": {\\n    \"verification_required\": true\\n  },\\n  \"legal_slots\": [\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Give the learner a reason to care and a concrete situation to hold.\",\\n      \"role\": \"orient\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"orient\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Reactivate the specific prior knowledge this lesson depends on. Nothing else.\",\\n      \"role\": \"recall\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"recall\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Show the method being carried out, with each step\\'s reasoning visible.\",\\n      \"role\": \"model\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"model\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Build the idea itself. State it, ground it, make it usable.\",\\n      \"role\": \"explain\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"explain\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Put a case and a near-miss side by side. The learner must see the boundary of the idea, not just the idea.\\\\n\",\\n      \"role\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"contrast\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Name the wrong belief, show why it feels right, then show it failing on a case. Correct exposition alone does not count.\\\\n\",\\n      \"role\": \"confront\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"confront\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Impose a structure on the facts so they are retrievable, not just listed.\",\\n      \"role\": \"organise\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"organise\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Establish what a good answer is judged against, before any case is seen.\",\\n      \"role\": \"criteria\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"criteria\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Practice with scaffolding still present. Learner does the thinking, support stays.\",\\n      \"role\": \"guided\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"guided\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Practice with scaffolding removed.\",\\n      \"role\": \"independent\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"independent\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Use the idea on a context not seen in this lesson.\",\\n      \"role\": \"apply\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"apply\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": true,\\n      \"purpose\": \"The shared diagnostic. Identical across every variant. Written from the card only, never from the prose above it.\\\\n\",\\n      \"role\": \"check\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"check\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Consolidate what was established and name what comes next.\",\\n      \"role\": \"close\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"close\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \"lesson_actuals\": [],\\n  \"max_slots\": 6,\\n  \"must_establish\": [\\n    \"inputs: light, water, carbon dioxide\",\\n    \"site: leaves\",\\n    \"outputs: food (sugar) and oxygen\",\\n    \"the food made is used by the plant to grow\"\\n  ],\\n  \"native_whole_lesson\": true,\\n  \"objective\": \"Explain how light, water and carbon dioxide combine in the leaves to make the food a plant needs to grow, naming the process as photosynthesis.\",\\n  \"objective_hash\": \"908d6eee5636618d2e1ec30ad5e2b6b2d03801ac8034029ed6609678e8b1fe7b\",\\n  \"prerequisites\": [\\n    {\\n      \"concept_id\": \"45a871de-8eb9-46e2-afae-40ba9daef901\",\\n      \"objective\": \"Explain, using evidence, that a plant needs light to make its food and that a plant without light cannot grow well.\",\\n      \"path_lesson_id\": \"9994a8b9-4976-42df-8c02-f7f241f7ba55\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"concept_id\": \"82b4d270-f860-4cb6-8745-0620ccf83951\",\\n      \"objective\": \"Identify water and carbon dioxide as the two raw materials a plant takes in to make food, and state where each is taken in.\",\\n      \"path_lesson_id\": \"09396f16-b468-49a1-ad39-758085855a39\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"concept_id\": \"ce26b085-651f-4ab6-8bf7-635a032f6a88\",\\n      \"objective\": \"Explain that the leaves are the part of the plant where food is made, because they receive light, water and carbon dioxide.\",\\n      \"path_lesson_id\": \"951c061d-a695-4308-9ef1-4082857b0b23\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"concept_id\": \"9a44988e-26fa-4f8b-a269-082cb5e9ae08\",\\n      \"objective\": \"Describe the outputs of the process \\\\u2014 food (sugar) used for growth and oxygen released into the air.\",\\n      \"path_lesson_id\": \"6c6ab8a7-3508-487d-a1dc-132a98d08206\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \"primary_knowledge_type\": \"evaluative\",\\n  \"prior_established\": [\\n    \"plants have roots, stems and leaves\",\\n    \"living things need food to grow\",\\n    \"plants produce their own food rather than absorbing it from soil\",\\n    \"soil supplies water and minerals, not food\",\\n    \"the food a plant makes is used for growth\",\\n    \"light is taken in by the plant and used as the energy source\",\\n    \"a plant kept in the dark cannot make food and will not thrive\",\\n    \"light energy is captured, not eaten\",\\n    \"water is taken in by the roots and carried to the leaves\",\\n    \"carbon dioxide is taken in from the air through the leaves\",\\n    \"these materials are changed, not simply stored\",\\n    \"leaves receive light and take in carbon dioxide\",\\n    \"water reaches the leaves from the roots\",\\n    \"food is made in the leaves and used or stored elsewhere\",\\n    \"the food made is a sugar used for growth and energy\",\\n    \"oxygen is produced and released\",\\n    \"the process is named photosynthesis\"\\n  ],\\n  \"recommended_slots\": [\\n    \"orient\",\\n    \"criteria\",\\n    \"contrast\",\\n    \"apply\",\\n    \"check\"\\n  ],\\n  \"scope_contract\": {\\n    \"assumed_prerequisites\": [],\\n    \"may_include\": [],\\n    \"must_establish\": [\\n      \"plants make their own food rather than taking it in ready-made\",\\n      \"light is required for plants to make food\",\\n      \"water and carbon dioxide are the raw materials\",\\n      \"leaves are the site where food is made\",\\n      \"the products of the process: food (sugar) and oxygen\"\\n    ],\\n    \"must_not_introduce\": [\\n      \"chemical equation for photosynthesis\",\\n      \"chlorophyll and chloroplasts as named structures\",\\n      \"light-dependent and light-independent reactions\",\\n      \"cellular respiration\"\\n    ],\\n    \"notation\": null,\\n    \"terminology\": [\\n      \"photosynthesis\",\\n      \"carbon dioxide\",\\n      \"oxygen\",\\n      \"light energy\",\\n      \"sugar\",\\n      \"leaves\"\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \"secondary_demand\": null,\\n  \"shared_preparation\": true,\\n  \"slots\": [\\n    {\\n      \"instance_id\": \"orient\",\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Give the learner a reason to care and a concrete situation to hold.\",\\n      \"role\": \"orient\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"orient\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"instance_id\": \"criteria\",\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Establish what a good answer is judged against, before any case is seen.\",\\n      \"role\": \"criteria\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"criteria\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"instance_id\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Put a case and a near-miss side by side. The learner must see the boundary of the idea, not just the idea.\\\\n\",\\n      \"role\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"contrast\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"instance_id\": \"apply\",\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Use the idea on a context not seen in this lesson.\",\\n      \"role\": \"apply\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"apply\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"instance_id\": \"check\",\\n      \"locked\": true,\\n      \"purpose\": \"The shared diagnostic. Identical across every variant. Written from the card only, never from the prose above it.\\\\n\",\\n      \"role\": \"check\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"check\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \"title\": \"Explaining how plants grow: putting the process together\",\\n  \"variant_previews\": [\\n    {\\n      \"group_profile\": \"core\",\\n      \"slots\": [\\n        {\\n          \"locked\": false,\\n          \"purp