{"timestamp": "2026-10-05T20:29:51.663370+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-9d696e89-cc19-47b9-b38d-6d15894fcd02', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': \"# Shared Section Writer\\n\\nWrite learner-facing display content for one Teaching Plan section. Composer owns the form. Preserve the supplied composition exactly:\\nreturn every ordinary node once, with its exact `id`, `kind`, and\\n`teaching_block_id`, in the supplied order. Do not output TaskAnchors; code\\ninserts them unchanged at their fixed positions.\\n\\nUse only the supplied section contract, block intent/evidence, approved facts,\\nsourcebook entries, terminology, evidence constraints, and compact finalized\\ntask summaries. Establish `must_establish`, respect `entry_state`, avoid\\nrepeating `avoid_repeating`, realize `bridge_from_previous`, and reach\\n`exit_state`. Distribute explanation across the nodes instead of making each\\nnode self-contained. Do not introduce unsupported facts or tasks.\\n\\nReturn only node `id`, `kind`, `teaching_block_id`, `display`, and\\n`accessibility` fields required by the output schema (figures have `display`\\nonly). Do not change structure,\\nwrite planning language or identifiers for learners, mention Learn or Print\\nimplementation, add placeholders, or include unsupported numeric values.\\nLists need meaningful non-empty items;\\ntables need non-empty headers and rows with matching column counts; callouts\\nneed a meaningful body. Key ideas use one bold sentence, notes stay concise,\\nand misconceptions use belief / evidence / conclusion fields. When the plan, brief\\nor packet names a misconception for the section and the composition has a\\nmisconception callout, write belief in the believer's own words, evidence that\\ntests it, and a conclusion stating the correct idea. Equations keep\\nevery input and output term, even when there are more than the display target;\\ncomparison nodes keep every card, even when there are more than three.\\n\\nShape prose rather than compressing it into one block: each paragraph holds\\none idea in three or four sentences and is normally at most 60 words; add a\\nsubheading when a section changes job or exceeds about 120 prose words; an\\nexplaining section opens with exactly one key idea. Code reserves the slot: when the\\npacket's `key_idea_slot_node_id` names a callout node, write exactly one `key_idea`\\ncallout there, one bold sentence of 25 words or fewer stating the section's main\\npoint; it is first in the section. If the composition has another\\ncallout node, it is a different callout; the key idea always\\ncomes before any equation, compare, table or figure, so when no callout opens the\\nsection, state it as one bold sentence in the first paragraph. Use lists only for steps\\nin order or parallel items of the same kind, and keep each list item near 30\\nwords. Keep table cells near 12 words, key ideas near 25 words, note bodies\\nnear 50 words, and misconception belief / evidence / conclusion near 30 / 45\\n/ 30 words. These are advisory targets: preserve all written words and every\\nterm/card if a target is exceeded. Never pad, truncate, rewrite, or retry to\\nhit a target.\\n\\nAll learner-facing strings may use the shared inline vocabulary: `**term**`\\nfor one key term, `*emphasis*`, `~subscript~`, `^superscript^`, and blank lines\\nfor paragraph breaks. Chemical formulas, units and exponents always use\\nthe inline markup (`CO~2~`, `H~2~O`, `C~6~H~12~O~6~`, `m^2^`, `cm^2^`), never\\nUnicode sub/superscripts or bare digits like CO2. Do not emit HTML, links,\\nheadings, lists, or unknown markup inside strings.\\n\\nFigures are placed by code from the block's `visual` spec in the section\\ncontract; never add, remove, or move one. For a `figure` node write only\\n`display.caption`; do not write alt text. The block's prose and the caption must\\nuse the exact `labels_required` and `must_show` wording from that `visual`:\\nnever rename, add, or drop any of it, and never mention `must_not_show` items.\\n\\nWhen a repair instruction is supplied, make only the indicated corrections\\nwhile preserving every valid node and its composed position. A section-aware\\nrepair should address the full section contract; a targeted repair should fix\\nonly the named node-level issues.\\n\\n## Hard rules\\n\\n- **Resolve every misconception you state.** If prose states a misconception,\\n  a wrong belief, or an incorrect reading (including ones drawn from a block's\\n  `brief` or the section's `must_establish`), the same section must explicitly\\n  correct it in the same breath or the very next sentence: say why it fails\\n  and state the correct understanding. Never state a wrong idea and move on\\n  without resolving it.\\n- **Never solve an anchored task.** `composition_plan` names which\\n  `task_spec_id` is anchored to which block via `task_anchor` items. Do not\\n  compute, solve, or state the answer, final value, or result of any task\\n  anchored anywhere in this section, before or after its anchor position. If\\n  you give a worked example or model calculation, it must use different\\n  numbers/values than the section's own tasks -- never the same problem the\\n  learner is about to be asked to solve.\\n- **`hidden_answer_context_do_not_reveal` is validator-only.** Its\\n  `expected_evidence` text explains what a correct learner response should\\n  demonstrate so you can judge whether your explanation sets the learner up\\n  to succeed. It is never learner-facing wording: never quote it, paraphrase\\n  it into a stated answer, or let it leak into `display`/`accessibility`\\n  text.\\n- **Stay factually accurate.** Do not state a simplification, generalization,\\n  or shortcut that is false, even if it reads simply. When simplifying,\\n  simplify the explanation, not the truth of the claim.\\n\"}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"$defs\": {\"CalloutDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"tone\": {\"default\": \"note\", \"enum\": [\"note\", \"warning\", \"tip\", \"important\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"body\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"variant\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"enum\": [\"key_idea\", \"note\", \"misconception\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"belief\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"evidence\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"conclusion\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"aside\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"title\": \"CalloutDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"CompareDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"items\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CompareItem\"}, \"minItems\": 2, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"items\"], \"title\": \"CompareDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"CompareItem\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"label\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"title\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"body\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"title\", \"body\"], \"title\": \"CompareItem\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"EquationDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"label\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"inputs\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"condition\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"outputs\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"inputs\", \"outputs\"], \"title\": \"EquationDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"FigureDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"asset_id\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"caption\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"title\": \"FigureDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"HeadingDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"text\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"level\": {\"default\": 2, \"maximum\": 3, \"minimum\": 1, \"type\": \"integer\"}}, \"required\": [\"text\"], \"title\": \"HeadingDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"ListDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"ordered\": {\"default\": false, \"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"items\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"items\"], \"title\": \"ListDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"NodeAccessibility\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"description\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"title\": \"NodeAccessibility\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"ParagraphDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"text\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"text\"], \"title\": \"ParagraphDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"QuoteDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"text\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"attribution\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"text\"], \"title\": \"QuoteDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"TableDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"headers\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"rows\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"caption\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"title\": \"TableDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenCallout\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"callout\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CalloutDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenCallout\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenCompare\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"compare\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CompareDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenCompare\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenEquation\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"equation\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/EquationDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenEquation\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenFigure\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"figure\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FigureDisplay\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenFigure\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenHeading\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"heading\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/HeadingDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenHeading\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenList\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"list\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ListDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenList\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenParagraph\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"paragraph\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ParagraphDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenParagraph\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenQuote\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"quote\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/QuoteDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenQuote\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenTable\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"table\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/TableDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenTable\", \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"nodes\": {\"items\": {\"discriminator\": {\"mapping\": {\"callout\": \"#/$defs/WrittenCallout\", \"compare\": \"#/$defs/WrittenCompare\", \"equation\": \"#/$defs/WrittenEquation\", \"figure\": \"#/$defs/WrittenFigure\", \"heading\": \"#/$defs/WrittenHeading\", \"list\": \"#/$defs/WrittenList\", \"paragraph\": \"#/$defs/WrittenParagraph\", \"quote\": \"#/$defs/WrittenQuote\", \"table\": \"#/$defs/WrittenTable\"}, \"propertyName\": \"kind\"}, \"oneOf\": [{\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenParagraph\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenHeading\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenList\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenFigure\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenTable\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenCallout\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenEquation\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenQuote\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenCompare\"}]}, \"minItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"nodes\"], \"title\": \"SectionWriterDraft\", \"type\": \"object\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{\"composition_plan\": [{\"id\": \"shared-key-idea-7fe844430e59f5140b20\", \"kind\": \"callout\", \"semantic_role\": \"explanation\", \"task_spec_id\": null, \"teaching_block_id\": \"criteria-b1\"}, {\"id\": \"shared-node-93018d86849e35fab26d\", \"kind\": \"paragraph\", \"semantic_role\": \"explanation\", \"task_spec_id\": null, \"teaching_block_id\": \"criteria-b1\"}, {\"id\": \"shared-figure-node-7fe844430e59f5140b20\", \"kind\": \"figure\", \"semantic_role\": \"visual_model\", \"task_spec_id\": null, \"teaching_block_id\": \"criteria-b1\"}], \"hidden_answer_context_do_not_reveal\": [], \"inline_vocabulary\": {\"emphasis\": \"*text*\", \"paragraph_break\": \"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\", \"strong\": \"**text**\", \"subscript\": \"~text~\", \"superscript\": \"^text^\"}, \"key_idea_slot_node_id\": \"shared-key-idea-7fe844430e59f5140b20\", \"repair\": null, \"section_contract\": {\"avoid_repeating\": [\"No re-description of the bean-plant pair beyond naming it as the case still waiting to be explained.\", \"No judgement yet about which accounts of growth fail.\"], \"blocks\": [{\"brief\": \"Give the precise definition the lesson will use: photosynthesis is the process in which light energy captured in the leaves combines water \\\\u2014 taken in by the roots and carried up the stem \\\\u2014 with carbon dioxide taken in from the air through the leaves, to make sugar, the plant\\'s food, and to release oxygen; that sugar is what the plant uses for growth and as an energy source. Then set the standard a complete explanation of a plant\\'s growth must meet: light, water and carbon dioxide named as the three inputs; the combining placed in the leaves; the product named as food, a sugar, used for growth; the process named photosynthesis. State that an explanation which credits the soil with supplying food or with supplying the material of new growth does not meet the standard. Do not explain the bean-plant pair yet.\", \"evidence\": \"The objective requires the learner to explain the process and name it, so the lesson must fix the definition and the acceptance standard before any case is judged, which is exactly what this slot places before a case is seen.\", \"id\": \"criteria-b1\", \"intent\": \"define\", \"visual\": {\"labels_required\": [\"light\", \"carbon dioxide\", \"water\", \"roots\", \"stem\", \"leaf\", \"sugar\", \"food\", \"oxygen\"], \"mode\": \"diagram\", \"must_not_show\": [\"soil supplying food or the material of new growth\", \"the plant taking oxygen in for food-making\", \"chemical formulas or equations\"], \"must_show\": [\"light reaching the leaf from the Sun\", \"carbon dioxide in the air entering the leaf\", \"water travelling from the roots up the stem into the leaf\", \"water and carbon dioxide combining inside the leaf, driven by light energy, to make sugar, the plant\\'s food\", \"sugar leaving the leaf to be used for growth and stored elsewhere in the plant\", \"oxygen being released from the leaf into the air as the sugar is made\"], \"purpose\": \"Show how light, water and carbon dioxide come together inside a leaf to make the sugar the plant uses for growth, and that oxygen leaves the leaf as this happens.\", \"required\": true}}], \"bridge_from_previous\": \"The opening left the pair\\'s growth unexplained and confirmed where each input enters the plant, so the lesson can now state the process those inputs take part in and the standard the explanation must meet.\", \"display_title\": \"What photosynthesis is, and what a full answer must contain\", \"entry_state\": [\"Learners hold the bean-plant difference as an open question.\", \"Learners can name the route of water, carbon dioxide and light into the plant.\"], \"exit_state\": [\"Learners can state what photosynthesis is, name the three inputs and the leaf as the site, and name the product as food used for growth.\", \"Learners can say what a complete explanation must include and what it must not credit.\"], \"must_establish\": [\"The definition of photosynthesis: light energy captured in the leaves combines water from the roots with carbon dioxide from the air to make sugar, the plant\\'s food, and to release oxygen; the sugar is what the plant uses for growth and as an energy source.\", \"The standard a complete explanation of a plant\\'s growth must meet: light, water and carbon dioxide named as the three inputs; the combining placed in the leaves; the product named as food, a sugar, used for growth; the process named photosynthesis; and no credit given to the soil for supplying food or the material of new growth.\"], \"specific_purpose\": \"Define photosynthesis precisely and fix the standard a complete explanation must meet, before the anchor pair is explained.\"}, \"shaping_targets\": {\"compare_items_target_max\": 3, \"equation_inputs_target_max\": 4, \"equation_outputs_target_max\": 3, \"key_idea_words_max\": 25, \"list_item_words_max\": 30, \"misconception_words_max\": {\"belief\": 30, \"conclusion\": 30, \"evidence\": 45}, \"note_words_max\": 50, \"paragraph_words_max\": 60, \"prose_section_words_target\": [150, 280], \"table_cell_words_max\": 12}, \"sources\": [], \"task_summaries\": []}'}], 'model': 'deepseek-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 16000, 'reasoning_effort': 'medium', 'stream': False}, 'extra_json': {'thinking': {'type': 'enabled'}}}"}
