{"timestamp": "2026-10-05T20:29:51.782888+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-d9d8664c-46d3-4459-8aaf-24f7a404203f', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': \"# Shared Section Writer\\n\\nWrite learner-facing display content for one Teaching Plan section. Composer owns the form. Preserve the supplied composition exactly:\\nreturn every ordinary node once, with its exact `id`, `kind`, and\\n`teaching_block_id`, in the supplied order. Do not output TaskAnchors; code\\ninserts them unchanged at their fixed positions.\\n\\nUse only the supplied section contract, block intent/evidence, approved facts,\\nsourcebook entries, terminology, evidence constraints, and compact finalized\\ntask summaries. Establish `must_establish`, respect `entry_state`, avoid\\nrepeating `avoid_repeating`, realize `bridge_from_previous`, and reach\\n`exit_state`. Distribute explanation across the nodes instead of making each\\nnode self-contained. Do not introduce unsupported facts or tasks.\\n\\nReturn only node `id`, `kind`, `teaching_block_id`, `display`, and\\n`accessibility` fields required by the output schema (figures have `display`\\nonly). Do not change structure,\\nwrite planning language or identifiers for learners, mention Learn or Print\\nimplementation, add placeholders, or include unsupported numeric values.\\nLists need meaningful non-empty items;\\ntables need non-empty headers and rows with matching column counts; callouts\\nneed a meaningful body. Key ideas use one bold sentence, notes stay concise,\\nand misconceptions use belief / evidence / conclusion fields. When the plan, brief\\nor packet names a misconception for the section and the composition has a\\nmisconception callout, write belief in the believer's own words, evidence that\\ntests it, and a conclusion stating the correct idea. Equations keep\\nevery input and output term, even when there are more than the display target;\\ncomparison nodes keep every card, even when there are more than three.\\n\\nShape prose rather than compressing it into one block: each paragraph holds\\none idea in three or four sentences and is normally at most 60 words; add a\\nsubheading when a section changes job or exceeds about 120 prose words; an\\nexplaining section opens with exactly one key idea. Code reserves the slot: when the\\npacket's `key_idea_slot_node_id` names a callout node, write exactly one `key_idea`\\ncallout there, one bold sentence of 25 words or fewer stating the section's main\\npoint; it is first in the section. If the composition has another\\ncallout node, it is a different callout; the key idea always\\ncomes before any equation, compare, table or figure, so when no callout opens the\\nsection, state it as one bold sentence in the first paragraph. Use lists only for steps\\nin order or parallel items of the same kind, and keep each list item near 30\\nwords. Keep table cells near 12 words, key ideas near 25 words, note bodies\\nnear 50 words, and misconception belief / evidence / conclusion near 30 / 45\\n/ 30 words. These are advisory targets: preserve all written words and every\\nterm/card if a target is exceeded. Never pad, truncate, rewrite, or retry to\\nhit a target.\\n\\nAll learner-facing strings may use the shared inline vocabulary: `**term**`\\nfor one key term, `*emphasis*`, `~subscript~`, `^superscript^`, and blank lines\\nfor paragraph breaks. Chemical formulas, units and exponents always use\\nthe inline markup (`CO~2~`, `H~2~O`, `C~6~H~12~O~6~`, `m^2^`, `cm^2^`), never\\nUnicode sub/superscripts or bare digits like CO2. Do not emit HTML, links,\\nheadings, lists, or unknown markup inside strings.\\n\\nFigures are placed by code from the block's `visual` spec in the section\\ncontract; never add, remove, or move one. For a `figure` node write only\\n`display.caption`; do not write alt text. The block's prose and the caption must\\nuse the exact `labels_required` and `must_show` wording from that `visual`:\\nnever rename, add, or drop any of it, and never mention `must_not_show` items.\\n\\nWhen a repair instruction is supplied, make only the indicated corrections\\nwhile preserving every valid node and its composed position. A section-aware\\nrepair should address the full section contract; a targeted repair should fix\\nonly the named node-level issues.\\n\\n## Hard rules\\n\\n- **Resolve every misconception you state.** If prose states a misconception,\\n  a wrong belief, or an incorrect reading (including ones drawn from a block's\\n  `brief` or the section's `must_establish`), the same section must explicitly\\n  correct it in the same breath or the very next sentence: say why it fails\\n  and state the correct understanding. Never state a wrong idea and move on\\n  without resolving it.\\n- **Never solve an anchored task.** `composition_plan` names which\\n  `task_spec_id` is anchored to which block via `task_anchor` items. Do not\\n  compute, solve, or state the answer, final value, or result of any task\\n  anchored anywhere in this section, before or after its anchor position. If\\n  you give a worked example or model calculation, it must use different\\n  numbers/values than the section's own tasks -- never the same problem the\\n  learner is about to be asked to solve.\\n- **`hidden_answer_context_do_not_reveal` is validator-only.** Its\\n  `expected_evidence` text explains what a correct learner response should\\n  demonstrate so you can judge whether your explanation sets the learner up\\n  to succeed. It is never learner-facing wording: never quote it, paraphrase\\n  it into a stated answer, or let it leak into `display`/`accessibility`\\n  text.\\n- **Stay factually accurate.** Do not state a simplification, generalization,\\n  or shortcut that is false, even if it reads simply. When simplifying,\\n  simplify the explanation, not the truth of the claim.\\n\"}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"$defs\": {\"CalloutDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"tone\": {\"default\": \"note\", \"enum\": [\"note\", \"warning\", \"tip\", \"important\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"body\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"variant\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"enum\": [\"key_idea\", \"note\", \"misconception\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"belief\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"evidence\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"conclusion\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"aside\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"title\": \"CalloutDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"CompareDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"items\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CompareItem\"}, \"minItems\": 2, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"items\"], \"title\": \"CompareDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"CompareItem\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"label\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"title\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"body\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"title\", \"body\"], \"title\": \"CompareItem\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"EquationDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"label\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"inputs\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"condition\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"outputs\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"inputs\", \"outputs\"], \"title\": \"EquationDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"FigureDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"asset_id\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"caption\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"title\": \"FigureDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"HeadingDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"text\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"level\": {\"default\": 2, \"maximum\": 3, \"minimum\": 1, \"type\": \"integer\"}}, \"required\": [\"text\"], \"title\": \"HeadingDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"ListDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"ordered\": {\"default\": false, \"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"items\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"items\"], \"title\": \"ListDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"NodeAccessibility\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"description\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"title\": \"NodeAccessibility\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"ParagraphDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"text\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"text\"], \"title\": \"ParagraphDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"QuoteDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"text\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"attribution\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"text\"], \"title\": \"QuoteDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"TableDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"headers\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"rows\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"caption\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"title\": \"TableDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenCallout\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"callout\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CalloutDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenCallout\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenCompare\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"compare\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CompareDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenCompare\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenEquation\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"equation\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/EquationDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenEquation\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenFigure\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"figure\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FigureDisplay\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenFigure\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenHeading\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"heading\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/HeadingDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenHeading\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenList\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"list\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ListDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenList\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenParagraph\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"paragraph\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ParagraphDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenParagraph\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenQuote\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"quote\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/QuoteDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenQuote\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenTable\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"table\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/TableDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenTable\", \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"nodes\": {\"items\": {\"discriminator\": {\"mapping\": {\"callout\": \"#/$defs/WrittenCallout\", \"compare\": \"#/$defs/WrittenCompare\", \"equation\": \"#/$defs/WrittenEquation\", \"figure\": \"#/$defs/WrittenFigure\", \"heading\": \"#/$defs/WrittenHeading\", \"list\": \"#/$defs/WrittenList\", \"paragraph\": \"#/$defs/WrittenParagraph\", \"quote\": \"#/$defs/WrittenQuote\", \"table\": \"#/$defs/WrittenTable\"}, \"propertyName\": \"kind\"}, \"oneOf\": [{\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenParagraph\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenHeading\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenList\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenFigure\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenTable\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenCallout\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenEquation\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenQuote\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenCompare\"}]}, \"minItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"nodes\"], \"title\": \"SectionWriterDraft\", \"type\": \"object\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{\"composition_plan\": [{\"id\": \"shared-node-8db81c2aad956244b743\", \"kind\": \"paragraph\", \"semantic_role\": \"bridge\", \"task_spec_id\": null, \"teaching_block_id\": \"orient-b1\"}, {\"id\": \"shared-node-6582509011cdc33ef8b1\", \"kind\": \"list\", \"semantic_role\": \"sequence\", \"task_spec_id\": null, \"teaching_block_id\": \"orient-b2\"}, {\"id\": \"shared-task-anchor-7cb468d182fda7b2e968\", \"kind\": \"task_anchor\", \"semantic_role\": null, \"task_spec_id\": \"task-orient-b2\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"orient-b2\"}], \"hidden_answer_context_do_not_reveal\": [{\"expected_evidence\": \"water paired with the roots and stem, carbon dioxide paired with the leaves and the air, light paired with the leaves\", \"task_spec_id\": \"task-orient-b2\"}], \"inline_vocabulary\": {\"emphasis\": \"*text*\", \"paragraph_break\": \"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\", \"strong\": \"**text**\", \"subscript\": \"~text~\", \"superscript\": \"^text^\"}, \"key_idea_slot_node_id\": null, \"repair\": null, \"section_contract\": {\"avoid_repeating\": [\"No statement of what the leaves do with the three inputs \\\\u2014 the definition belongs to the next section.\", \"No explanation of why the cupboard plant failed to grow.\"], \"blocks\": [{\"brief\": \"Open on the anchor pair: two bean plants from the same batch in identical pots of the same soil, watered the same amount on the same days. One stands on a sunny windowsill, its twin in a dark cupboard. After two weeks the windowsill plant is taller, greener and carrying new leaves; the cupboard plant is pale, short and has added no new leaves. Set out only what was held the same and what was observed, and leave the cause open: state that both plants received the same water and the same soil, and ask what the windowsill plant used to build its new stem and leaves. Do not say that light is the answer, do not explain what a leaf does with anything, and do not call either account of the difference correct or incorrect.\", \"evidence\": \"The slot asks for a concrete situation to hold, and the anchor pair is that situation; describing the two plants and their divergence without the cause gives the learner something the later mechanism has to resolve.\", \"id\": \"orient-b1\", \"intent\": \"orient\", \"visual\": null}, {\"brief\": \"Recall the three things a plant relies on and how each reaches it: water is taken in by the roots from the soil and carried up the stem to the leaves; carbon dioxide is taken in from the air through the leaves; light is captured by the leaves. Also recall that the soil supplies only water and minerals, never food. Keep this to what learners already know, and stop before saying what the leaves do with the water and the carbon dioxide.\", \"evidence\": \"The combining step later in the lesson is impossible to follow unless the learner has the three inputs and their routes live in memory, and this recall is brief and diagnostic rather than new teaching.\", \"id\": \"orient-b2\", \"intent\": \"activate-prior-knowledge\", \"visual\": null}], \"bridge_from_previous\": null, \"display_title\": \"Two bean plants, one difference\", \"entry_state\": [\"Learners know a plant has roots, stems and leaves and that a plant makes its own food rather than taking food from the soil.\", \"Learners know soil supplies water and minerals, and that light is needed for a plant to thrive, but they have not combined these into an account of how food is made.\"], \"exit_state\": [\"Learners hold the bean-plant pair and its unexplained difference in growth.\", \"Learners can say where water, carbon dioxide and light each enter or are captured by a plant.\"], \"must_establish\": [\"The anchor observation: two bean plants in identical pots of the same soil, watered the same amount on the same days, one on a sunny windowsill and one in a dark cupboard; after two weeks only the windowsill plant is taller, greener and carrying new leaves.\", \"That water is taken in by the roots and carried up the stem to the leaves, carbon dioxide is taken in from the air through the leaves, and light is captured by the leaves.\"], \"specific_purpose\": \"Open on the anchor pair and get the three inputs into play as routes learners already know.\"}, \"shaping_targets\": {\"compare_items_target_max\": 3, \"equation_inputs_target_max\": 4, \"equation_outputs_target_max\": 3, \"key_idea_words_max\": 25, \"list_item_words_max\": 30, \"misconception_words_max\": {\"belief\": 30, \"conclusion\": 30, \"evidence\": 45}, \"note_words_max\": 50, \"paragraph_words_max\": 60, \"prose_section_words_target\": [150, 280], \"table_cell_words_max\": 12}, \"sources\": [], \"task_summaries\": [{\"action\": \"match-pairs\", \"prompt\": \"Match each thing the plant relies on with how it reaches or is captured by the plant. Water is taken in by the roots from the soil and carried up the stem to the leaves; carbon dioxide is taken in from the air through the leaves; light is captured by the leaves.\", \"purpose\": \"retrieve the route of each input before the inputs are combined in the leaves\", \"task_spec_id\": \"task-orient-b2\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"orient-b2\"}]}'}], 'model': 'deepseek-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 16000, 'reasoning_effort': 'medium', 'stream': False}, 'extra_json': {'thinking': {'type': 'enabled'}}}"}
