{"timestamp": "2026-10-05T20:29:52.363458+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-062736e5-381c-442d-9f73-b158c5e03eb1', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': \"# Shared Section Writer\\n\\nWrite learner-facing display content for one Teaching Plan section. Composer owns the form. Preserve the supplied composition exactly:\\nreturn every ordinary node once, with its exact `id`, `kind`, and\\n`teaching_block_id`, in the supplied order. Do not output TaskAnchors; code\\ninserts them unchanged at their fixed positions.\\n\\nUse only the supplied section contract, block intent/evidence, approved facts,\\nsourcebook entries, terminology, evidence constraints, and compact finalized\\ntask summaries. Establish `must_establish`, respect `entry_state`, avoid\\nrepeating `avoid_repeating`, realize `bridge_from_previous`, and reach\\n`exit_state`. Distribute explanation across the nodes instead of making each\\nnode self-contained. Do not introduce unsupported facts or tasks.\\n\\nReturn only node `id`, `kind`, `teaching_block_id`, `display`, and\\n`accessibility` fields required by the output schema (figures have `display`\\nonly). Do not change structure,\\nwrite planning language or identifiers for learners, mention Learn or Print\\nimplementation, add placeholders, or include unsupported numeric values.\\nLists need meaningful non-empty items;\\ntables need non-empty headers and rows with matching column counts; callouts\\nneed a meaningful body. Key ideas use one bold sentence, notes stay concise,\\nand misconceptions use belief / evidence / conclusion fields. When the plan, brief\\nor packet names a misconception for the section and the composition has a\\nmisconception callout, write belief in the believer's own words, evidence that\\ntests it, and a conclusion stating the correct idea. Equations keep\\nevery input and output term, even when there are more than the display target;\\ncomparison nodes keep every card, even when there are more than three.\\n\\nShape prose rather than compressing it into one block: each paragraph holds\\none idea in three or four sentences and is normally at most 60 words; add a\\nsubheading when a section changes job or exceeds about 120 prose words; an\\nexplaining section opens with exactly one key idea. Code reserves the slot: when the\\npacket's `key_idea_slot_node_id` names a callout node, write exactly one `key_idea`\\ncallout there, one bold sentence of 25 words or fewer stating the section's main\\npoint; it is first in the section. If the composition has another\\ncallout node, it is a different callout; the key idea always\\ncomes before any equation, compare, table or figure, so when no callout opens the\\nsection, state it as one bold sentence in the first paragraph. Use lists only for steps\\nin order or parallel items of the same kind, and keep each list item near 30\\nwords. Keep table cells near 12 words, key ideas near 25 words, note bodies\\nnear 50 words, and misconception belief / evidence / conclusion near 30 / 45\\n/ 30 words. These are advisory targets: preserve all written words and every\\nterm/card if a target is exceeded. Never pad, truncate, rewrite, or retry to\\nhit a target.\\n\\nAll learner-facing strings may use the shared inline vocabulary: `**term**`\\nfor one key term, `*emphasis*`, `~subscript~`, `^superscript^`, and blank lines\\nfor paragraph breaks. Chemical formulas, units and exponents always use\\nthe inline markup (`CO~2~`, `H~2~O`, `C~6~H~12~O~6~`, `m^2^`, `cm^2^`), never\\nUnicode sub/superscripts or bare digits like CO2. Do not emit HTML, links,\\nheadings, lists, or unknown markup inside strings.\\n\\nFigures are placed by code from the block's `visual` spec in the section\\ncontract; never add, remove, or move one. For a `figure` node write only\\n`display.caption`; do not write alt text. The block's prose and the caption must\\nuse the exact `labels_required` and `must_show` wording from that `visual`:\\nnever rename, add, or drop any of it, and never mention `must_not_show` items.\\n\\nWhen a repair instruction is supplied, make only the indicated corrections\\nwhile preserving every valid node and its composed position. A section-aware\\nrepair should address the full section contract; a targeted repair should fix\\nonly the named node-level issues.\\n\\n## Hard rules\\n\\n- **Resolve every misconception you state.** If prose states a misconception,\\n  a wrong belief, or an incorrect reading (including ones drawn from a block's\\n  `brief` or the section's `must_establish`), the same section must explicitly\\n  correct it in the same breath or the very next sentence: say why it fails\\n  and state the correct understanding. Never state a wrong idea and move on\\n  without resolving it.\\n- **Never solve an anchored task.** `composition_plan` names which\\n  `task_spec_id` is anchored to which block via `task_anchor` items. Do not\\n  compute, solve, or state the answer, final value, or result of any task\\n  anchored anywhere in this section, before or after its anchor position. If\\n  you give a worked example or model calculation, it must use different\\n  numbers/values than the section's own tasks -- never the same problem the\\n  learner is about to be asked to solve.\\n- **`hidden_answer_context_do_not_reveal` is validator-only.** Its\\n  `expected_evidence` text explains what a correct learner response should\\n  demonstrate so you can judge whether your explanation sets the learner up\\n  to succeed. It is never learner-facing wording: never quote it, paraphrase\\n  it into a stated answer, or let it leak into `display`/`accessibility`\\n  text.\\n- **Stay factually accurate.** Do not state a simplification, generalization,\\n  or shortcut that is false, even if it reads simply. When simplifying,\\n  simplify the explanation, not the truth of the claim.\\n\"}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"$defs\": {\"CalloutDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"tone\": {\"default\": \"note\", \"enum\": [\"note\", \"warning\", \"tip\", \"important\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"body\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"variant\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"enum\": [\"key_idea\", \"note\", \"misconception\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"belief\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"evidence\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"conclusion\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"aside\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"title\": \"CalloutDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"CompareDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"items\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CompareItem\"}, \"minItems\": 2, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"items\"], \"title\": \"CompareDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"CompareItem\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"label\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"title\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"body\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"title\", \"body\"], \"title\": \"CompareItem\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"EquationDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"label\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"inputs\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"condition\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"outputs\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"inputs\", \"outputs\"], \"title\": \"EquationDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"FigureDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"asset_id\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"caption\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"title\": \"FigureDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"HeadingDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"text\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"level\": {\"default\": 2, \"maximum\": 3, \"minimum\": 1, \"type\": \"integer\"}}, \"required\": [\"text\"], \"title\": \"HeadingDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"ListDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"ordered\": {\"default\": false, \"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"items\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"items\"], \"title\": \"ListDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"NodeAccessibility\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"description\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"title\": \"NodeAccessibility\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"ParagraphDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"text\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"text\"], \"title\": \"ParagraphDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"QuoteDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"text\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"attribution\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"text\"], \"title\": \"QuoteDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"TableDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"headers\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"rows\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"caption\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"title\": \"TableDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenCallout\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"callout\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CalloutDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenCallout\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenCompare\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"compare\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CompareDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenCompare\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenEquation\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"equation\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/EquationDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenEquation\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenFigure\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"figure\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FigureDisplay\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenFigure\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenHeading\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"heading\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/HeadingDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenHeading\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenList\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"list\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ListDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenList\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenParagraph\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"paragraph\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ParagraphDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenParagraph\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenQuote\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"quote\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/QuoteDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenQuote\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenTable\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"table\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/TableDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenTable\", \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"nodes\": {\"items\": {\"discriminator\": {\"mapping\": {\"callout\": \"#/$defs/WrittenCallout\", \"compare\": \"#/$defs/WrittenCompare\", \"equation\": \"#/$defs/WrittenEquation\", \"figure\": \"#/$defs/WrittenFigure\", \"heading\": \"#/$defs/WrittenHeading\", \"list\": \"#/$defs/WrittenList\", \"paragraph\": \"#/$defs/WrittenParagraph\", \"quote\": \"#/$defs/WrittenQuote\", \"table\": \"#/$defs/WrittenTable\"}, \"propertyName\": \"kind\"}, \"oneOf\": [{\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenParagraph\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenHeading\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenList\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenFigure\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenTable\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenCallout\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenEquation\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenQuote\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenCompare\"}]}, \"minItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"nodes\"], \"title\": \"SectionWriterDraft\", \"type\": \"object\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{\"composition_plan\": [{\"id\": \"shared-node-b8284177470216edc90b\", \"kind\": \"paragraph\", \"semantic_role\": \"bridge\", \"task_spec_id\": null, \"teaching_block_id\": \"apply-b1\"}, {\"id\": \"shared-node-8cd71a77b870ea8ae553\", \"kind\": \"paragraph\", \"semantic_role\": \"explanation\", \"task_spec_id\": null, \"teaching_block_id\": \"apply-b1\"}, {\"id\": \"shared-task-anchor-04f09b3df21b782567ac\", \"kind\": \"task_anchor\", \"semantic_role\": null, \"task_spec_id\": \"task-apply-b1\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"apply-b1\"}, {\"id\": \"shared-node-16ccb904f979e9db405c\", \"kind\": \"paragraph\", \"semantic_role\": \"explanation\", \"task_spec_id\": null, \"teaching_block_id\": \"apply-b2\"}, {\"id\": \"shared-task-anchor-2de690ba39afe8ea62cf\", \"kind\": \"task_anchor\", \"semantic_role\": null, \"task_spec_id\": \"task-apply-b2\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"apply-b2\"}], \"hidden_answer_context_do_not_reveal\": [{\"expected_evidence\": \"an explanation naming carbon dioxide entering the leaves, water from the roots, light energy captured in the leaves and sugar used for growth, and stating that with too little light the extra carbon dioxide cannot be combined\", \"task_spec_id\": \"task-apply-b1\"}, {\"expected_evidence\": \"an explanation that less light reaches the leaves, so less light energy is captured, less carbon dioxide and water are combined into sugar, and less food is available for new growth\", \"task_spec_id\": \"task-apply-b2\"}], \"inline_vocabulary\": {\"emphasis\": \"*text*\", \"paragraph_break\": \"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\", \"strong\": \"**text**\", \"subscript\": \"~text~\", \"superscript\": \"^text^\"}, \"key_idea_slot_node_id\": null, \"repair\": null, \"section_contract\": {\"avoid_repeating\": [\"No re-use of the bean-plant pair, the definition or the standard.\", \"No prompts in the second situation.\"], \"blocks\": [{\"brief\": \"Present a greenhouse of tomato vines on a bright summer morning: the grower raises the amount of carbon dioxide in the greenhouse air and the vines put on growth faster than before; on a dull, heavily overcast day the same extra carbon dioxide makes almost no difference. Prompt the learner through the reasoning without finishing it: name where the extra carbon dioxide enters the plant, name what else has to be present, and say what the leaves do with the carbon dioxide and the water when light is available. Supply the prompts, not the completed explanation.\", \"evidence\": \"The apply slot requires a context the lesson has not used, and this situation forces the learner to hold all three inputs together while varying only light, which the anchor pair did not ask them to state in words.\", \"id\": \"apply-b1\", \"intent\": \"practise-guided\", \"visual\": null}, {\"brief\": \"Present a second situation the lesson has not used: a broad-leaved houseplant in a bright room has its leaves coated with a thick layer of dust, and over the following weeks it puts on far less new growth than before, although it is watered exactly as before and the room stays just as bright. With nothing but the situation to work from, the learner explains the slowdown: less light reaches the leaves, so the leaves capture less light energy and combine less carbon dioxide and water into sugar, so less food is available for building new growth. Do not name the answer and do not restate the definition.\", \"evidence\": \"The learner has just succeeded with prompts, so the same mechanism must now be produced without them on a situation whose only change is the light reaching the leaves, which is the cleanest unaided test short of the check itself.\", \"id\": \"apply-b2\", \"intent\": \"practise-independent\", \"visual\": null}], \"bridge_from_previous\": \"The mechanism has been explained and defended on the bean-plant pair, so learners can now run it on cases the lesson has not used.\", \"display_title\": \"Using the idea somewhere new\", \"entry_state\": [\"Learners can explain the pair\\'s growth by the mechanism and reject the three failing accounts.\", \"Learners can name the three inputs, the leaf as the site and sugar as the product.\"], \"exit_state\": [\"Learners can explain a bright-light greenhouse and a dust-covered houseplant by the inputs, the leaf site, the sugar produced and the light energy that drives the combining.\", \"Learners can produce the second explanation unaided.\"], \"must_establish\": [\"That extra carbon dioxide speeds a greenhouse crop only when there is enough light for the leaves to combine it with water into sugar.\", \"That anything reducing the light reaching the leaves reduces the sugar made and therefore the new growth, even when the water and the carbon dioxide are unchanged.\"], \"specific_purpose\": \"Run the mechanism on two situations the lesson has not used, first with prompts and then unaided.\"}, \"shaping_targets\": {\"compare_items_target_max\": 3, \"equation_inputs_target_max\": 4, \"equation_outputs_target_max\": 3, \"key_idea_words_max\": 25, \"list_item_words_max\": 30, \"misconception_words_max\": {\"belief\": 30, \"conclusion\": 30, \"evidence\": 45}, \"note_words_max\": 50, \"paragraph_words_max\": 60, \"prose_section_words_target\": [150, 280], \"table_cell_words_max\": 12}, \"sources\": [], \"task_summaries\": [{\"action\": \"enter-text\", \"prompt\": \"In a greenhouse of tomato vines on a bright summer morning, the grower raises the amount of carbon dioxide in the air and the vines put on growth faster than before. On a dull, heavily overcast day the same extra carbon dioxide makes almost no difference. Explain why added carbon dioxide speeds growth on a bright morning but not on a dull day. Name where the extra carbon dioxide enters the plant, what else has to be present, and what the leaves do with the carbon dioxide and the water when light is available.\", \"purpose\": \"first supported use of the mechanism on a situation the lesson has not used\", \"task_spec_id\": \"task-apply-b1\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"apply-b1\"}, {\"action\": \"enter-text\", \"prompt\": \"A broad-leaved houseplant in a bright room has its leaves coated with a thick layer of dust. Over the following weeks it puts on far less new growth than before, although it is watered exactly as before and the room stays just as bright. Using only the situation, explain why the plant\\'s growth has slowed.\", \"purpose\": \"unaided use of the mechanism on a second unseen situation\", \"task_spec_id\": \"task-apply-b2\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"apply-b2\"}]}'}], 'model': 'deepseek-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 16000, 'reasoning_effort': 'medium', 'stream': False}, 'extra_json': {'thinking': {'type': 'enabled'}}}"}
