{"timestamp": "2026-10-05T20:29:52.505714+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-74baf6ad-200f-45d1-b032-27cea21f541f', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': \"# Shared Section Writer\\n\\nWrite learner-facing display content for one Teaching Plan section. Composer owns the form. Preserve the supplied composition exactly:\\nreturn every ordinary node once, with its exact `id`, `kind`, and\\n`teaching_block_id`, in the supplied order. Do not output TaskAnchors; code\\ninserts them unchanged at their fixed positions.\\n\\nUse only the supplied section contract, block intent/evidence, approved facts,\\nsourcebook entries, terminology, evidence constraints, and compact finalized\\ntask summaries. Establish `must_establish`, respect `entry_state`, avoid\\nrepeating `avoid_repeating`, realize `bridge_from_previous`, and reach\\n`exit_state`. Distribute explanation across the nodes instead of making each\\nnode self-contained. Do not introduce unsupported facts or tasks.\\n\\nReturn only node `id`, `kind`, `teaching_block_id`, `display`, and\\n`accessibility` fields required by the output schema (figures have `display`\\nonly). Do not change structure,\\nwrite planning language or identifiers for learners, mention Learn or Print\\nimplementation, add placeholders, or include unsupported numeric values.\\nLists need meaningful non-empty items;\\ntables need non-empty headers and rows with matching column counts; callouts\\nneed a meaningful body. Key ideas use one bold sentence, notes stay concise,\\nand misconceptions use belief / evidence / conclusion fields. When the plan, brief\\nor packet names a misconception for the section and the composition has a\\nmisconception callout, write belief in the believer's own words, evidence that\\ntests it, and a conclusion stating the correct idea. Equations keep\\nevery input and output term, even when there are more than the display target;\\ncomparison nodes keep every card, even when there are more than three.\\n\\nShape prose rather than compressing it into one block: each paragraph holds\\none idea in three or four sentences and is normally at most 60 words; add a\\nsubheading when a section changes job or exceeds about 120 prose words; an\\nexplaining section opens with exactly one key idea. Code reserves the slot: when the\\npacket's `key_idea_slot_node_id` names a callout node, write exactly one `key_idea`\\ncallout there, one bold sentence of 25 words or fewer stating the section's main\\npoint; it is first in the section. If the composition has another\\ncallout node, it is a different callout; the key idea always\\ncomes before any equation, compare, table or figure, so when no callout opens the\\nsection, state it as one bold sentence in the first paragraph. Use lists only for steps\\nin order or parallel items of the same kind, and keep each list item near 30\\nwords. Keep table cells near 12 words, key ideas near 25 words, note bodies\\nnear 50 words, and misconception belief / evidence / conclusion near 30 / 45\\n/ 30 words. These are advisory targets: preserve all written words and every\\nterm/card if a target is exceeded. Never pad, truncate, rewrite, or retry to\\nhit a target.\\n\\nAll learner-facing strings may use the shared inline vocabulary: `**term**`\\nfor one key term, `*emphasis*`, `~subscript~`, `^superscript^`, and blank lines\\nfor paragraph breaks. Chemical formulas, units and exponents always use\\nthe inline markup (`CO~2~`, `H~2~O`, `C~6~H~12~O~6~`, `m^2^`, `cm^2^`), never\\nUnicode sub/superscripts or bare digits like CO2. Do not emit HTML, links,\\nheadings, lists, or unknown markup inside strings.\\n\\nFigures are placed by code from the block's `visual` spec in the section\\ncontract; never add, remove, or move one. For a `figure` node write only\\n`display.caption`; do not write alt text. The block's prose and the caption must\\nuse the exact `labels_required` and `must_show` wording from that `visual`:\\nnever rename, add, or drop any of it, and never mention `must_not_show` items.\\n\\nWhen a repair instruction is supplied, make only the indicated corrections\\nwhile preserving every valid node and its composed position. A section-aware\\nrepair should address the full section contract; a targeted repair should fix\\nonly the named node-level issues.\\n\\n## Hard rules\\n\\n- **Resolve every misconception you state.** If prose states a misconception,\\n  a wrong belief, or an incorrect reading (including ones drawn from a block's\\n  `brief` or the section's `must_establish`), the same section must explicitly\\n  correct it in the same breath or the very next sentence: say why it fails\\n  and state the correct understanding. Never state a wrong idea and move on\\n  without resolving it.\\n- **Never solve an anchored task.** `composition_plan` names which\\n  `task_spec_id` is anchored to which block via `task_anchor` items. Do not\\n  compute, solve, or state the answer, final value, or result of any task\\n  anchored anywhere in this section, before or after its anchor position. If\\n  you give a worked example or model calculation, it must use different\\n  numbers/values than the section's own tasks -- never the same problem the\\n  learner is about to be asked to solve.\\n- **`hidden_answer_context_do_not_reveal` is validator-only.** Its\\n  `expected_evidence` text explains what a correct learner response should\\n  demonstrate so you can judge whether your explanation sets the learner up\\n  to succeed. It is never learner-facing wording: never quote it, paraphrase\\n  it into a stated answer, or let it leak into `display`/`accessibility`\\n  text.\\n- **Stay factually accurate.** Do not state a simplification, generalization,\\n  or shortcut that is false, even if it reads simply. When simplifying,\\n  simplify the explanation, not the truth of the claim.\\n\"}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"$defs\": {\"CalloutDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"tone\": {\"default\": \"note\", \"enum\": [\"note\", \"warning\", \"tip\", \"important\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"body\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"variant\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"enum\": [\"key_idea\", \"note\", \"misconception\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"belief\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"evidence\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"conclusion\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"aside\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"title\": \"CalloutDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"CompareDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"items\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CompareItem\"}, \"minItems\": 2, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"items\"], \"title\": \"CompareDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"CompareItem\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"label\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"title\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"body\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"title\", \"body\"], \"title\": \"CompareItem\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"EquationDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"label\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"inputs\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"condition\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"outputs\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"inputs\", \"outputs\"], \"title\": \"EquationDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"FigureDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"asset_id\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"caption\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"title\": \"FigureDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"HeadingDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"text\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"level\": {\"default\": 2, \"maximum\": 3, \"minimum\": 1, \"type\": \"integer\"}}, \"required\": [\"text\"], \"title\": \"HeadingDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"ListDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"ordered\": {\"default\": false, \"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"items\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"items\"], \"title\": \"ListDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"NodeAccessibility\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"description\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"title\": \"NodeAccessibility\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"ParagraphDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"text\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"text\"], \"title\": \"ParagraphDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"QuoteDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"text\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"attribution\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"text\"], \"title\": \"QuoteDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"TableDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"headers\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"rows\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"caption\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"title\": \"TableDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenCallout\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"callout\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CalloutDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenCallout\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenCompare\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"compare\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CompareDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenCompare\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenEquation\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"equation\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/EquationDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenEquation\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenFigure\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"figure\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FigureDisplay\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenFigure\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenHeading\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"heading\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/HeadingDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenHeading\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenList\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"list\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ListDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenList\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenParagraph\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"paragraph\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ParagraphDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenParagraph\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenQuote\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"quote\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/QuoteDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenQuote\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenTable\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"table\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/TableDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenTable\", \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"nodes\": {\"items\": {\"discriminator\": {\"mapping\": {\"callout\": \"#/$defs/WrittenCallout\", \"compare\": \"#/$defs/WrittenCompare\", \"equation\": \"#/$defs/WrittenEquation\", \"figure\": \"#/$defs/WrittenFigure\", \"heading\": \"#/$defs/WrittenHeading\", \"list\": \"#/$defs/WrittenList\", \"paragraph\": \"#/$defs/WrittenParagraph\", \"quote\": \"#/$defs/WrittenQuote\", \"table\": \"#/$defs/WrittenTable\"}, \"propertyName\": \"kind\"}, \"oneOf\": [{\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenParagraph\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenHeading\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenList\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenFigure\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenTable\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenCallout\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenEquation\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenQuote\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenCompare\"}]}, \"minItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"nodes\"], \"title\": \"SectionWriterDraft\", \"type\": \"object\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{\"composition_plan\": [{\"id\": \"shared-key-idea-dc0d5a021ecf27ece901\", \"kind\": \"callout\", \"semantic_role\": \"explanation\", \"task_spec_id\": null, \"teaching_block_id\": \"contrast-b1\"}, {\"id\": \"shared-node-9eef5f7e8590911e8a8b\", \"kind\": \"callout\", \"semantic_role\": \"misconception\", \"task_spec_id\": null, \"teaching_block_id\": \"contrast-b1\"}, {\"id\": \"shared-task-anchor-be51521b23581d0c80da\", \"kind\": \"task_anchor\", \"semantic_role\": null, \"task_spec_id\": \"task-contrast-b1\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"contrast-b1\"}, {\"id\": \"shared-node-dcfaa39ede0c1e623c54\", \"kind\": \"paragraph\", \"semantic_role\": \"explanation\", \"task_spec_id\": null, \"teaching_block_id\": \"contrast-b2\"}, {\"id\": \"shared-node-ff6c81d8bad6f602a745\", \"kind\": \"callout\", \"semantic_role\": \"misconception\", \"task_spec_id\": null, \"teaching_block_id\": \"contrast-b3\"}], \"hidden_answer_context_do_not_reveal\": [{\"expected_evidence\": \"an explanation that identical soil and identical water rule the soil account out, so the difference must lie in something the windowsill plant had and the cupboard plant did not\", \"task_spec_id\": \"task-contrast-b1\"}], \"inline_vocabulary\": {\"emphasis\": \"*text*\", \"paragraph_break\": \"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\", \"strong\": \"**text**\", \"subscript\": \"~text~\", \"superscript\": \"^text^\"}, \"key_idea_slot_node_id\": \"shared-key-idea-dc0d5a021ecf27ece901\", \"repair\": null, \"section_contract\": {\"avoid_repeating\": [\"No restating of the definition of photosynthesis or of the standard.\", \"No re-use of the bean-plant pair in later sections.\"], \"blocks\": [{\"brief\": \"Name the account that the new stem and leaves were built from material supplied by the soil, with water and light only helping the plant along. State plainly what is correct instead: the soil supplies water and minerals and nothing else, so it does not supply food and does not supply the material of new growth; the plant builds that material from the sugar it makes in its leaves by combining carbon dioxide from the air with water from the roots. Show the account failing on the pair: the cupboard plant stood in the same soil and was watered exactly as the windowsill plant was, yet it built no new growth at all, so soil and water cannot be what made the difference.\", \"evidence\": \"The soil account is a held belief with a confident wrong answer, so it must be named and shown failing rather than merely flagged as a slip; the anchor pair\\'s identical soil and water supply the falsifying evidence inside the case the lesson already uses.\", \"id\": \"contrast-b1\", \"intent\": \"diagnose-misconception\", \"visual\": null}, {\"brief\": \"Explain the pair\\'s outcome by the mechanism: the windowsill plant\\'s leaves captured light energy, and inside those leaves water from the roots was combined with carbon dioxide from the air to make sugar, and that sugar was used to build the taller stem, the greener leaves and the new growth. The cupboard plant had the same soil and the same water, and carbon dioxide was present in the air around it, but with no light its leaves could not combine them, so no sugar was made and no new growth was built. State plainly what is wrong with treating light and carbon dioxide as mere comfort conditions: carbon dioxide is a raw material, and its atoms become part of the sugar the plant makes; light supplies the energy that drives the combining, and that energy ends up stored in the sugar. Show the account failing: if light and carbon dioxide were only comfort conditions, the cupboard plant \\\\u2014 which had water, soil and air \\\\u2014 would have grown as well.\", \"evidence\": \"The objective asks how the three inputs combine to make food, which is a mechanism linking cause to result; only a causal account of the pair can show why the same water and soil produced two different outcomes, and it is also what makes the comfort-condition account fail.\", \"id\": \"contrast-b2\", \"intent\": \"explain-cause\", \"visual\": null}, {\"brief\": \"Name the account that the plant takes oxygen in to make its food. State plainly what is correct instead: when water and carbon dioxide are combined into sugar in the leaves, oxygen is produced and released from the leaves into the air, so making food gives oxygen out rather than taking it in. Show the account failing: in bright light the leaves of a leafy plant give out oxygen, so the air around such a plant gains oxygen rather than losing it \\\\u2014 the opposite of what the account predicts.\", \"evidence\": \"The direction oxygen moves is a specific, confidently held error about the products of food-making, so it needs the wrong direction named and contradicted by the evidence, which a general statement that oxygen is released would not do.\", \"id\": \"contrast-b3\", \"intent\": \"diagnose-misconception\", \"visual\": null}], \"bridge_from_previous\": \"The definition and the standard are now available, so the pair\\'s outcome can be explained causally and each competing account can be checked against the standard.\", \"display_title\": \"Explaining the two plants \\\\u2014 and the accounts that fail\", \"entry_state\": [\"Learners can state the definition of photosynthesis and the standard a complete explanation must meet.\", \"Learners hold the pair\\'s outcome and know that light was the one condition that differed.\"], \"exit_state\": [\"Learners can explain the pair\\'s growth by the mechanism and say what the cupboard plant was missing.\", \"Learners can state why the soil account, the comfort-condition account and the oxygen-intake account fail.\"], \"must_establish\": [\"The causal account of the pair: the windowsill plant\\'s leaves captured light energy and combined water with carbon dioxide to make sugar, and that sugar built the taller stem, the greener leaves and the new growth; the cupboard plant had the same soil and water and carbon dioxide in the air around it, but no light energy, so no sugar was made and no new growth was built.\", \"The correct understanding behind each failing account: soil supplies only water and minerals, never food or growth material; carbon dioxide\\'s atoms become part of the sugar and light supplies the energy that drives the combining and is stored in the sugar, so neither is a comfort condition; and oxygen is produced and released from the leaves as the sugar is made, not taken in for it.\"], \"specific_purpose\": \"Explain the anchor pair by the mechanism and show the three wrong accounts failing against the standard.\"}, \"shaping_targets\": {\"compare_items_target_max\": 3, \"equation_inputs_target_max\": 4, \"equation_outputs_target_max\": 3, \"key_idea_words_max\": 25, \"list_item_words_max\": 30, \"misconception_words_max\": {\"belief\": 30, \"conclusion\": 30, \"evidence\": 45}, \"note_words_max\": 50, \"paragraph_words_max\": 60, \"prose_section_words_target\": [150, 280], \"table_cell_words_max\": 12}, \"sources\": [], \"task_summaries\": [{\"action\": \"enter-text\", \"prompt\": \"Someone claims that the new stem and leaves of the windowsill bean plant were built from material supplied by the soil, with water and light only helping the plant along. The cupboard plant stood in the same soil and was watered exactly as the windowsill plant was, yet it built no new growth at all. Explain why identical soil and identical watering cannot account for the difference between the two plants.\", \"purpose\": \"make the learner produce the refutation rather than recognise it\", \"task_spec_id\": \"task-contrast-b1\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"contrast-b1\"}]}'}], 'model': 'deepseek-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 16000, 'reasoning_effort': 'medium', 'stream': False}, 'extra_json': {'thinking': {'type': 'enabled'}}}"}
