{"timestamp": "2026-10-05T20:30:10.107264+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-3d9fd39d-5440-4730-ba06-672fb077e118', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': \"# Shared Section Writer\\n\\nWrite learner-facing display content for one Teaching Plan section. Composer owns the form. Preserve the supplied composition exactly:\\nreturn every ordinary node once, with its exact `id`, `kind`, and\\n`teaching_block_id`, in the supplied order. Do not output TaskAnchors; code\\ninserts them unchanged at their fixed positions.\\n\\nUse only the supplied section contract, block intent/evidence, approved facts,\\nsourcebook entries, terminology, evidence constraints, and compact finalized\\ntask summaries. Establish `must_establish`, respect `entry_state`, avoid\\nrepeating `avoid_repeating`, realize `bridge_from_previous`, and reach\\n`exit_state`. Distribute explanation across the nodes instead of making each\\nnode self-contained. Do not introduce unsupported facts or tasks.\\n\\nReturn only node `id`, `kind`, `teaching_block_id`, `display`, and\\n`accessibility` fields required by the output schema (figures have `display`\\nonly). Do not change structure,\\nwrite planning language or identifiers for learners, mention Learn or Print\\nimplementation, add placeholders, or include unsupported numeric values.\\nLists need meaningful non-empty items;\\ntables need non-empty headers and rows with matching column counts; callouts\\nneed a meaningful body. Key ideas use one bold sentence, notes stay concise,\\nand misconceptions use belief / evidence / conclusion fields. When the plan, brief\\nor packet names a misconception for the section and the composition has a\\nmisconception callout, write belief in the believer's own words, evidence that\\ntests it, and a conclusion stating the correct idea. Equations keep\\nevery input and output term, even when there are more than the display target;\\ncomparison nodes keep every card, even when there are more than three.\\n\\nShape prose rather than compressing it into one block: each paragraph holds\\none idea in three or four sentences and is normally at most 60 words; add a\\nsubheading when a section changes job or exceeds about 120 prose words; an\\nexplaining section opens with exactly one key idea. Code reserves the slot: when the\\npacket's `key_idea_slot_node_id` names a callout node, write exactly one `key_idea`\\ncallout there, one bold sentence of 25 words or fewer stating the section's main\\npoint; it is first in the section. If the composition has another\\ncallout node, it is a different callout; the key idea always\\ncomes before any equation, compare, table or figure, so when no callout opens the\\nsection, state it as one bold sentence in the first paragraph. Use lists only for steps\\nin order or parallel items of the same kind, and keep each list item near 30\\nwords. Keep table cells near 12 words, key ideas near 25 words, note bodies\\nnear 50 words, and misconception belief / evidence / conclusion near 30 / 45\\n/ 30 words. These are advisory targets: preserve all written words and every\\nterm/card if a target is exceeded. Never pad, truncate, rewrite, or retry to\\nhit a target.\\n\\nAll learner-facing strings may use the shared inline vocabulary: `**term**`\\nfor one key term, `*emphasis*`, `~subscript~`, `^superscript^`, and blank lines\\nfor paragraph breaks. Chemical formulas, units and exponents always use\\nthe inline markup (`CO~2~`, `H~2~O`, `C~6~H~12~O~6~`, `m^2^`, `cm^2^`), never\\nUnicode sub/superscripts or bare digits like CO2. Do not emit HTML, links,\\nheadings, lists, or unknown markup inside strings.\\n\\nFigures are placed by code from the block's `visual` spec in the section\\ncontract; never add, remove, or move one. For a `figure` node write only\\n`display.caption`; do not write alt text. The block's prose and the caption must\\nuse the exact `labels_required` and `must_show` wording from that `visual`:\\nnever rename, add, or drop any of it, and never mention `must_not_show` items.\\n\\nWhen a repair instruction is supplied, make only the indicated corrections\\nwhile preserving every valid node and its composed position. A section-aware\\nrepair should address the full section contract; a targeted repair should fix\\nonly the named node-level issues.\\n\\n## Hard rules\\n\\n- **Resolve every misconception you state.** If prose states a misconception,\\n  a wrong belief, or an incorrect reading (including ones drawn from a block's\\n  `brief` or the section's `must_establish`), the same section must explicitly\\n  correct it in the same breath or the very next sentence: say why it fails\\n  and state the correct understanding. Never state a wrong idea and move on\\n  without resolving it.\\n- **Never solve an anchored task.** `composition_plan` names which\\n  `task_spec_id` is anchored to which block via `task_anchor` items. Do not\\n  compute, solve, or state the answer, final value, or result of any task\\n  anchored anywhere in this section, before or after its anchor position. If\\n  you give a worked example or model calculation, it must use different\\n  numbers/values than the section's own tasks -- never the same problem the\\n  learner is about to be asked to solve.\\n- **`hidden_answer_context_do_not_reveal` is validator-only.** Its\\n  `expected_evidence` text explains what a correct learner response should\\n  demonstrate so you can judge whether your explanation sets the learner up\\n  to succeed. It is never learner-facing wording: never quote it, paraphrase\\n  it into a stated answer, or let it leak into `display`/`accessibility`\\n  text.\\n- **Stay factually accurate.** Do not state a simplification, generalization,\\n  or shortcut that is false, even if it reads simply. When simplifying,\\n  simplify the explanation, not the truth of the claim.\\n\"}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"$defs\": {\"CalloutDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"tone\": {\"default\": \"note\", \"enum\": [\"note\", \"warning\", \"tip\", \"important\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"body\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"variant\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"enum\": [\"key_idea\", \"note\", \"misconception\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"belief\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"evidence\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"conclusion\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"aside\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"title\": \"CalloutDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"CompareDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"items\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CompareItem\"}, \"minItems\": 2, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"items\"], \"title\": \"CompareDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"CompareItem\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"label\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"title\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"body\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"title\", \"body\"], \"title\": \"CompareItem\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"EquationDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"label\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"inputs\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"condition\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"outputs\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"inputs\", \"outputs\"], \"title\": \"EquationDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"FigureDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"asset_id\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"caption\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"title\": \"FigureDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"HeadingDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"text\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"level\": {\"default\": 2, \"maximum\": 3, \"minimum\": 1, \"type\": \"integer\"}}, \"required\": [\"text\"], \"title\": \"HeadingDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"ListDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"ordered\": {\"default\": false, \"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"items\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"items\"], \"title\": \"ListDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"NodeAccessibility\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"description\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"title\": \"NodeAccessibility\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"ParagraphDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"text\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"text\"], \"title\": \"ParagraphDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"QuoteDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"text\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"attribution\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"text\"], \"title\": \"QuoteDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"TableDisplay\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"headers\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"rows\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"caption\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"title\": \"TableDisplay\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenCallout\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"callout\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CalloutDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenCallout\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenCompare\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"compare\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CompareDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenCompare\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenEquation\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"equation\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/EquationDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenEquation\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenFigure\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"figure\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FigureDisplay\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenFigure\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenHeading\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"heading\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/HeadingDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenHeading\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenList\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"list\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ListDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenList\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenParagraph\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"paragraph\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ParagraphDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenParagraph\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenQuote\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"quote\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/QuoteDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenQuote\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"WrittenTable\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"teaching_block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"const\": \"table\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"display\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/TableDisplay\"}, \"accessibility\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NodeAccessibility\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"teaching_block_id\", \"kind\", \"display\"], \"title\": \"WrittenTable\", \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"nodes\": {\"items\": {\"discriminator\": {\"mapping\": {\"callout\": \"#/$defs/WrittenCallout\", \"compare\": \"#/$defs/WrittenCompare\", \"equation\": \"#/$defs/WrittenEquation\", \"figure\": \"#/$defs/WrittenFigure\", \"heading\": \"#/$defs/WrittenHeading\", \"list\": \"#/$defs/WrittenList\", \"paragraph\": \"#/$defs/WrittenParagraph\", \"quote\": \"#/$defs/WrittenQuote\", \"table\": \"#/$defs/WrittenTable\"}, \"propertyName\": \"kind\"}, \"oneOf\": [{\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenParagraph\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenHeading\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenList\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenFigure\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenTable\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenCallout\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenEquation\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenQuote\"}, {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/WrittenCompare\"}]}, \"minItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"nodes\"], \"title\": \"SectionWriterDraft\", \"type\": \"object\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{\"composition_plan\": [{\"id\": \"shared-node-de29f59a1337f2019e9c\", \"kind\": \"paragraph\", \"semantic_role\": \"evidence\", \"task_spec_id\": null, \"teaching_block_id\": \"check-b1\"}, {\"id\": \"shared-task-anchor-6e75dcdbcc26c575163c\", \"kind\": \"task_anchor\", \"semantic_role\": null, \"task_spec_id\": \"task-check-b1\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"check-b1\"}], \"hidden_answer_context_do_not_reveal\": [{\"expected_evidence\": \"selects the explanation that places food-making in the leaves from water and carbon dioxide using light, rather than an explanation that credits soil or another outside source with supplying the growth material\", \"task_spec_id\": \"task-check-b1\"}], \"inline_vocabulary\": {\"emphasis\": \"*text*\", \"paragraph_break\": \"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\", \"strong\": \"**text**\", \"subscript\": \"~text~\", \"superscript\": \"^text^\"}, \"key_idea_slot_node_id\": null, \"repair\": null, \"section_contract\": {\"avoid_repeating\": [\"No reminder of the definition, the standard or the bean-plant pair before the check.\", \"No hint, feedback or re-teaching inside the check.\"], \"blocks\": [{\"brief\": \"Administer the approved item bound to this block, with no prompts, no reminder of the definition or the standard, and no reference to the bean-plant pair, so the selection shows the learner\\'s own explanation of how the plant gains mass. Record the single selection as it stands, without correcting it while the learner is working.\", \"evidence\": \"The check slot is the lesson\\'s measurement point and this approved item asks for the explanation of growth the objective targets, so binding it here and nowhere else keeps its scenario out of the teaching sections and lets the selection stand as evidence of the learner\\'s model.\", \"id\": \"check-b1\", \"intent\": \"check-understanding\", \"visual\": null}], \"bridge_from_previous\": \"The apply section showed the mechanism working with support and then without it, so the check can now measure the same explanation with nothing supplied.\", \"display_title\": \"Check: what explains a plant\\'s growth\", \"entry_state\": [\"Learners have explained two situations the lesson did not use, the first with prompts and the second without.\", \"Learners know the three inputs, the leaf as the site, the sugar as the product and the name of the process.\"], \"exit_state\": [\"The teacher can identify which learners hold the mechanism and which still explain growth by material taken from outside the plant.\"], \"must_establish\": [\"An unaided selection showing whether the learner explains the plant\\'s growth by food made in the leaves from water and carbon dioxide using light, or by material taken from outside the plant.\"], \"specific_purpose\": \"Measure, with no help, whether learners explain growth by food made in the leaves rather than by material taken from outside the plant.\"}, \"shaping_targets\": {\"compare_items_target_max\": 3, \"equation_inputs_target_max\": 4, \"equation_outputs_target_max\": 3, \"key_idea_words_max\": 25, \"list_item_words_max\": 30, \"misconception_words_max\": {\"belief\": 30, \"conclusion\": 30, \"evidence\": 45}, \"note_words_max\": 50, \"paragraph_words_max\": 60, \"prose_section_words_target\": [150, 280], \"table_cell_words_max\": 12}, \"sources\": [], \"task_summaries\": [{\"action\": \"select-one\", \"prompt\": \"A potted plant is placed where its leaves can get light, but its roots sit in pure water with no soil at all. The plant still gains mass over several weeks. Which statement best explains the plant\\'s growth?\", \"purpose\": \"measure whether the learner explains growth by food made in the leaves rather than by material taken from outside the plant\", \"task_spec_id\": \"task-check-b1\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"check-b1\"}]}'}], 'model': 'deepseek-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 16000, 'reasoning_effort': 'medium', 'stream': False}, 'extra_json': {'thinking': {'type': 'enabled'}}}"}
