{"timestamp": "2026-10-05T20:30:47.083449+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-69214e63-8a28-41fc-9078-91ebf817eb65', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': '# Shared Section Boundary Validator\\n\\nReview the boundary between two already accepted shared lesson sections.\\nUse only the supplied previous section exit state and final nodes, and the\\nnext section entry state, bridge, and first nodes. Return exactly one of:\\n\\n```json\\n{\"status\":\"pass\"}\\n```\\n\\nor a typed issue:\\n\\n```json\\n{\"status\":\"issue\",\"issue\":{\"issue_code\":\"...\",\"affected_section_id\":\"...\",\"affected_node_ids\":[],\"explanation\":\"...\",\"required_correction\":\"...\"}}\\n```\\n\\nThe issue must target the previous or next section in the supplied boundary.\\nDescribe the continuity defect and the smallest learner-facing correction.\\nJudge meaning, not word overlap: paraphrases of an approved bridge, entry\\nstate, or exit state count as covered when the supplied nodes clearly express\\nthe same idea. Return an issue only when the needed idea is genuinely missing,\\ncontradicted, or too weak to support the next section.\\nDo not write replacement section content. Do not mention internal IDs,\\ncomposition plans, renderer paths, Learn, Print, model planning, or this\\nreview process in the issue text.\\n'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"$defs\": {\"ContinuityIssue\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"A typed, actionable QA result. Validators never rewrite content.\", \"properties\": {\"issue_code\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"affected_section_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"affected_node_ids\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"explanation\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"required_correction\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"issue_code\", \"affected_section_id\", \"explanation\", \"required_correction\"], \"title\": \"ContinuityIssue\", \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"status\": {\"enum\": [\"pass\", \"issue\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"issue\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ContinuityIssue\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"status\"], \"title\": \"BoundarySemanticVerdict\", \"type\": \"object\", \"description\": \"Closed reviewer output: exactly PASS or one typed continuity issue.\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{\"next_bridge\": \"The apply section showed the mechanism working with support and then without it, so the check can now measure the same explanation with nothing supplied.\", \"next_entry_state\": [\"Learners have explained two situations the lesson did not use, the first with prompts and the second without.\", \"Learners know the three inputs, the leaf as the site, the sugar as the product and the name of the process.\"], \"next_first_nodes\": [{\"accessibility\": {\"description\": \"Short instruction telling the learner to read the question and choose the single best explanation on their own, before the check item opens.\"}, \"display\": {\"text\": \"One question follows. Read it carefully and choose the single explanation you think is best. Answer on your own, without looking back at earlier sections, and give the reason you actually believe rather than the one you think is wanted.\"}, \"id\": \"shared-node-de29f59a1337f2019e9c\", \"kind\": \"paragraph\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"check-b1\"}, {\"id\": \"shared-task-anchor-6e75dcdbcc26c575163c\", \"kind\": \"task_anchor\", \"role\": null, \"task_spec_id\": \"task-check-b1\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"check-b1\"}], \"next_plan\": {\"avoid_repeating\": [\"No reminder of the definition, the standard or the bean-plant pair before the check.\", \"No hint, feedback or re-teaching inside the check.\"], \"blocks\": [{\"brief\": \"Administer the approved item bound to this block, with no prompts, no reminder of the definition or the standard, and no reference to the bean-plant pair, so the selection shows the learner\\'s own explanation of how the plant gains mass. Record the single selection as it stands, without correcting it while the learner is working.\", \"departure_reason\": null, \"evidence\": \"The check slot is the lesson\\'s measurement point and this approved item asks for the explanation of growth the objective targets, so binding it here and nowhere else keeps its scenario out of the teaching sections and lets the selection stand as evidence of the learner\\'s model.\", \"evidence_refs\": [\"slot.check.purpose\", \"lesson.objective\", \"item.910bef47-fcc3-4eca-a8a4-845c986d2d99:910bef47-fcc3-4eca-a8a4-845c986d2d99:9704c8b6-3b96-49d1-ade2-ad4c55329be1.i3\"], \"id\": \"check-b1\", \"intent\": \"check-understanding\", \"learner_action\": {\"action\": \"select-one\", \"difficulty\": \"independent\", \"expected_evidence\": \"selects the explanation that places food-making in the leaves from water and carbon dioxide using light, rather than an explanation that credits soil or another outside source with supplying the growth material\", \"purpose\": \"measure whether the learner explains growth by food made in the leaves rather than by material taken from outside the plant\", \"target\": \"the explanation of how the plant gains mass\"}, \"position\": 0, \"source_question_ids\": [\"910bef47-fcc3-4eca-a8a4-845c986d2d99:910bef47-fcc3-4eca-a8a4-845c986d2d99:9704c8b6-3b96-49d1-ade2-ad4c55329be1.i3\"], \"sourcebook_needs\": [], \"sourcebook_refs\": [], \"stimulus_dependencies\": [], \"task_mode\": \"assessment\"}], \"bridge_from_previous\": \"The apply section showed the mechanism working with support and then without it, so the check can now measure the same explanation with nothing supplied.\", \"display_title\": \"Check: what explains a plant\\'s growth\", \"entry_state\": [\"Learners have explained two situations the lesson did not use, the first with prompts and the second without.\", \"Learners know the three inputs, the leaf as the site, the sugar as the product and the name of the process.\"], \"exit_state\": [\"The teacher can identify which learners hold the mechanism and which still explain growth by material taken from outside the plant.\"], \"must_establish\": [\"An unaided selection showing whether the learner explains the plant\\'s growth by food made in the leaves from water and carbon dioxide using light, or by material taken from outside the plant.\"], \"slot_id\": \"check\", \"specific_purpose\": \"Measure, with no help, whether learners explain growth by food made in the leaves rather than by material taken from outside the plant.\", \"transition\": \"The lesson closes here, and the record of who still uses a soil or comfort-condition account shows what to reteach before the class moves on to how the sugar a plant makes is transported and used.\"}, \"previous_exit_state\": [\"Learners can explain a bright-light greenhouse and a dust-covered houseplant by the inputs, the leaf site, the sugar produced and the light energy that drives the combining.\", \"Learners can produce the second explanation unaided.\"], \"previous_final_nodes\": [{\"id\": \"shared-task-anchor-04f09b3df21b782567ac\", \"kind\": \"task_anchor\", \"role\": null, \"task_spec_id\": \"task-apply-b1\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"apply-b1\"}, {\"accessibility\": {\"description\": \"\"}, \"display\": {\"text\": \"Now apply the same reasoning without prompts. The next case changes only the light reaching the leaves. Your explanation should trace that change through the chain of inputs, leaf action, and growth.\"}, \"id\": \"shared-node-16ccb904f979e9db405c\", \"kind\": \"paragraph\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"apply-b2\"}, {\"id\": \"shared-task-anchor-2de690ba39afe8ea62cf\", \"kind\": \"task_anchor\", \"role\": null, \"task_spec_id\": \"task-apply-b2\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"apply-b2\"}], \"previous_plan\": {\"avoid_repeating\": [\"No re-use of the bean-plant pair, the definition or the standard.\", \"No prompts in the second situation.\"], \"blocks\": [{\"brief\": \"Present a greenhouse of tomato vines on a bright summer morning: the grower raises the amount of carbon dioxide in the greenhouse air and the vines put on growth faster than before; on a dull, heavily overcast day the same extra carbon dioxide makes almost no difference. Prompt the learner through the reasoning without finishing it: name where the extra carbon dioxide enters the plant, name what else has to be present, and say what the leaves do with the carbon dioxide and the water when light is available. Supply the prompts, not the completed explanation.\", \"departure_reason\": \"The apply slot has no typical intents, and the learner needs a supported first attempt on an unseen situation before any unaided work, so practise-guided is the fitting permitted intent rather than a second explanation by the teacher.\", \"evidence\": \"The apply slot requires a context the lesson has not used, and this situation forces the learner to hold all three inputs together while varying only light, which the anchor pair did not ask them to state in words.\", \"evidence_refs\": [\"lesson.objective\", \"slot.apply.purpose\"], \"id\": \"apply-b1\", \"intent\": \"practise-guided\", \"learner_action\": {\"action\": \"enter-text\", \"difficulty\": \"guided\", \"expected_evidence\": \"an explanation naming carbon dioxide entering the leaves, water from the roots, light energy captured in the leaves and sugar used for growth, and stating that with too little light the extra carbon dioxide cannot be combined\", \"purpose\": \"first supported use of the mechanism on a situation the lesson has not used\", \"target\": \"why added carbon dioxide speeds growth on a bright morning but not on a dull day\"}, \"position\": 0, \"source_question_ids\": [], \"sourcebook_needs\": [], \"sourcebook_refs\": [], \"stimulus_dependencies\": [], \"task_mode\": \"formative\"}, {\"brief\": \"Present a second situation the lesson has not used: a broad-leaved houseplant in a bright room has its leaves coated with a thick layer of dust, and over the following weeks it puts on far less new growth than before, although it is watered exactly as before and the room stays just as bright. With nothing but the situation to work from, the learner explains the slowdown: less light reaches the leaves, so the leaves capture less light energy and combine less carbon dioxide and water into sugar, so less food is available for building new growth. Do not name the answer and do not restate the definition.\", \"departure_reason\": \"The apply slot has no typical intents, and after a supported attempt the learner must perform unaided; stopping at guided practice would leave the lesson without any independent use of the mechanism.\", \"evidence\": \"The learner has just succeeded with prompts, so the same mechanism must now be produced without them on a situation whose only change is the light reaching the leaves, which is the cleanest unaided test short of the check itself.\", \"evidence_refs\": [\"slot.apply.purpose\", \"prior-14\", \"lesson.objective\"], \"id\": \"apply-b2\", \"intent\": \"practise-independent\", \"learner_action\": {\"action\": \"enter-text\", \"difficulty\": \"independent\", \"expected_evidence\": \"an explanation that less light reaches the leaves, so less light energy is captured, less carbon dioxide and water are combined into sugar, and less food is available for new growth\", \"purpose\": \"unaided use of the mechanism on a second unseen situation\", \"target\": \"why a dust-covered houseplant in a bright room slows its growth while its watering is unchanged\"}, \"position\": 1, \"source_question_ids\": [], \"sourcebook_needs\": [], \"sourcebook_refs\": [], \"stimulus_dependencies\": [], \"task_mode\": \"formative\"}], \"bridge_from_previous\": \"The mechanism has been explained and defended on the bean-plant pair, so learners can now run it on cases the lesson has not used.\", \"display_title\": \"Using the idea somewhere new\", \"entry_state\": [\"Learners can explain the pair\\'s growth by the mechanism and reject the three failing accounts.\", \"Learners can name the three inputs, the leaf as the site and sugar as the product.\"], \"exit_state\": [\"Learners can explain a bright-light greenhouse and a dust-covered houseplant by the inputs, the leaf site, the sugar produced and the light energy that drives the combining.\", \"Learners can produce the second explanation unaided.\"], \"must_establish\": [\"That extra carbon dioxide speeds a greenhouse crop only when there is enough light for the leaves to combine it with water into sugar.\", \"That anything reducing the light reaching the leaves reduces the sugar made and therefore the new growth, even when the water and the carbon dioxide are unchanged.\"], \"slot_id\": \"apply\", \"specific_purpose\": \"Run the mechanism on two situations the lesson has not used, first with prompts and then unaided.\", \"transition\": \"The final step measures whether that explanation is in place with no support at all.\"}}'}], 'model': 'deepseek-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 16000, 'stream': False}, 'extra_json': {'thinking': {'type': 'disabled'}}}"}
