{"timestamp": "2026-10-05T20:30:47.214381+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-6cd9c805-7a17-4560-8687-2eb40efa389e', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': '# Shared Section Boundary Validator\\n\\nReview the boundary between two already accepted shared lesson sections.\\nUse only the supplied previous section exit state and final nodes, and the\\nnext section entry state, bridge, and first nodes. Return exactly one of:\\n\\n```json\\n{\"status\":\"pass\"}\\n```\\n\\nor a typed issue:\\n\\n```json\\n{\"status\":\"issue\",\"issue\":{\"issue_code\":\"...\",\"affected_section_id\":\"...\",\"affected_node_ids\":[],\"explanation\":\"...\",\"required_correction\":\"...\"}}\\n```\\n\\nThe issue must target the previous or next section in the supplied boundary.\\nDescribe the continuity defect and the smallest learner-facing correction.\\nJudge meaning, not word overlap: paraphrases of an approved bridge, entry\\nstate, or exit state count as covered when the supplied nodes clearly express\\nthe same idea. Return an issue only when the needed idea is genuinely missing,\\ncontradicted, or too weak to support the next section.\\nDo not write replacement section content. Do not mention internal IDs,\\ncomposition plans, renderer paths, Learn, Print, model planning, or this\\nreview process in the issue text.\\n'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"$defs\": {\"ContinuityIssue\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"A typed, actionable QA result. Validators never rewrite content.\", \"properties\": {\"issue_code\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"affected_section_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"affected_node_ids\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"explanation\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"required_correction\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"issue_code\", \"affected_section_id\", \"explanation\", \"required_correction\"], \"title\": \"ContinuityIssue\", \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"status\": {\"enum\": [\"pass\", \"issue\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"issue\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ContinuityIssue\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"status\"], \"title\": \"BoundarySemanticVerdict\", \"type\": \"object\", \"description\": \"Closed reviewer output: exactly PASS or one typed continuity issue.\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{\"next_bridge\": \"The opening left the pair\\'s growth unexplained and confirmed where each input enters the plant, so the lesson can now state the process those inputs take part in and the standard the explanation must meet.\", \"next_entry_state\": [\"Learners hold the bean-plant difference as an open question.\", \"Learners can name the route of water, carbon dioxide and light into the plant.\"], \"next_first_nodes\": [{\"accessibility\": {\"description\": \"Key idea: photosynthesis combines water and carbon dioxide in leaves using light energy to make sugar and release oxygen.\"}, \"display\": {\"body\": \"**Photosynthesis is the process in which leaves use light energy to combine water and carbon dioxide into sugar, the plant\\'s food, releasing oxygen.**\", \"title\": \"\", \"tone\": \"note\", \"variant\": \"key_idea\"}, \"id\": \"shared-key-idea-7fe844430e59f5140b20\", \"kind\": \"callout\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"criteria-b1\"}, {\"accessibility\": {\"description\": \"Defines photosynthesis, names the three inputs and the leaf as the site, names the product as food used for growth, sets the standard for a complete explanation, and corrects the idea that soil supplies food or the material of new growth.\"}, \"display\": {\"text\": \"Photosynthesis is the process in which light energy captured in the leaves combines water with carbon dioxide to make sugar, the plant\\'s food, and to release oxygen. The water is taken in by the roots and carried up the stem; carbon dioxide enters the leaves from the air. This sugar is the plant\\'s food, used for growth and as an energy source.\\\\n\\\\nA complete explanation of a plant\\'s growth must meet a clear standard. It must name light, water and carbon dioxide as the three inputs, place the combining in the leaves, name the product as food, a sugar, used for growth, and name the process photosynthesis.\\\\n\\\\nAn explanation that credits the soil with supplying food, or with supplying the material of new growth, does not meet the standard. The soil supplies water and dissolved minerals; the sugar the plant uses for growth is made inside the leaf, from water and carbon dioxide, using light energy.\\\\n\\\\nThe bean-plant case from the opening is still waiting to be explained.\"}, \"id\": \"shared-node-93018d86849e35fab26d\", \"kind\": \"paragraph\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"criteria-b1\"}, {\"accessibility\": {\"alt_text\": \"\"}, \"display\": {\"asset_id\": null, \"caption\": \"The diagram shows light reaching the leaf from the Sun, carbon dioxide in the air entering the leaf, and water travelling from the roots up the stem into the leaf. It also shows water and carbon dioxide combining inside the leaf, driven by light energy, to make sugar, the plant\\'s food, sugar leaving the leaf to be used for growth and stored elsewhere in the plant, and oxygen being released from the leaf into the air as the sugar is made.\"}, \"id\": \"shared-figure-node-7fe844430e59f5140b20\", \"kind\": \"figure\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"criteria-b1\"}], \"next_plan\": {\"avoid_repeating\": [\"No re-description of the bean-plant pair beyond naming it as the case still waiting to be explained.\", \"No judgement yet about which accounts of growth fail.\"], \"blocks\": [{\"brief\": \"Give the precise definition the lesson will use: photosynthesis is the process in which light energy captured in the leaves combines water \\\\u2014 taken in by the roots and carried up the stem \\\\u2014 with carbon dioxide taken in from the air through the leaves, to make sugar, the plant\\'s food, and to release oxygen; that sugar is what the plant uses for growth and as an energy source. Then set the standard a complete explanation of a plant\\'s growth must meet: light, water and carbon dioxide named as the three inputs; the combining placed in the leaves; the product named as food, a sugar, used for growth; the process named photosynthesis. State that an explanation which credits the soil with supplying food or with supplying the material of new growth does not meet the standard. Do not explain the bean-plant pair yet.\", \"departure_reason\": \"The criteria slot supplies no typical intents, so the slot\\'s own job \\\\u2014 establishing the definition and the standard \\\\u2014 has to be carried by a permitted intent that fixes meaning precisely, and define is the only permitted intent written for that.\", \"evidence\": \"The objective requires the learner to explain the process and name it, so the lesson must fix the definition and the acceptance standard before any case is judged, which is exactly what this slot places before a case is seen.\", \"evidence_refs\": [\"lesson.objective\", \"prior-17\", \"prior-4\", \"prior-16\", \"slot.criteria.purpose\"], \"id\": \"criteria-b1\", \"intent\": \"define\", \"learner_action\": null, \"position\": 0, \"source_question_ids\": [], \"sourcebook_needs\": [], \"sourcebook_refs\": [], \"stimulus_dependencies\": [], \"task_mode\": \"none\", \"visual\": {\"labels_required\": [\"light\", \"carbon dioxide\", \"water\", \"roots\", \"stem\", \"leaf\", \"sugar\", \"food\", \"oxygen\"], \"mode\": \"diagram\", \"must_not_show\": [\"soil supplying food or the material of new growth\", \"the plant taking oxygen in for food-making\", \"chemical formulas or equations\"], \"must_show\": [\"light reaching the leaf from the Sun\", \"carbon dioxide in the air entering the leaf\", \"water travelling from the roots up the stem into the leaf\", \"water and carbon dioxide combining inside the leaf, driven by light energy, to make sugar, the plant\\'s food\", \"sugar leaving the leaf to be used for growth and stored elsewhere in the plant\", \"oxygen being released from the leaf into the air as the sugar is made\"], \"purpose\": \"Show how light, water and carbon dioxide come together inside a leaf to make the sugar the plant uses for growth, and that oxygen leaves the leaf as this happens.\", \"required\": true}}], \"bridge_from_previous\": \"The opening left the pair\\'s growth unexplained and confirmed where each input enters the plant, so the lesson can now state the process those inputs take part in and the standard the explanation must meet.\", \"display_title\": \"What photosynthesis is, and what a full answer must contain\", \"entry_state\": [\"Learners hold the bean-plant difference as an open question.\", \"Learners can name the route of water, carbon dioxide and light into the plant.\"], \"exit_state\": [\"Learners can state what photosynthesis is, name the three inputs and the leaf as the site, and name the product as food used for growth.\", \"Learners can say what a complete explanation must include and what it must not credit.\"], \"must_establish\": [\"The definition of photosynthesis: light energy captured in the leaves combines water from the roots with carbon dioxide from the air to make sugar, the plant\\'s food, and to release oxygen; the sugar is what the plant uses for growth and as an energy source.\", \"The standard a complete explanation of a plant\\'s growth must meet: light, water and carbon dioxide named as the three inputs; the combining placed in the leaves; the product named as food, a sugar, used for growth; the process named photosynthesis; and no credit given to the soil for supplying food or the material of new growth.\"], \"slot_id\": \"criteria\", \"specific_purpose\": \"Define photosynthesis precisely and fix the standard a complete explanation must meet, before the anchor pair is explained.\", \"transition\": \"With the definition and the standard fixed, the lesson returns to the bean-plant pair to explain it and to test the accounts that fail.\"}, \"previous_exit_state\": [\"Learners hold the bean-plant pair and its unexplained difference in growth.\", \"Learners can say where water, carbon dioxide and light each enter or are captured by a plant.\"], \"previous_final_nodes\": [{\"accessibility\": {\"description\": \"Two bean plants in identical pots of the same soil, watered the same amount on the same days, one on a sunny windowsill and one in a dark cupboard. After two weeks, the windowsill plant is taller, greener and has new leaves, while the cupboard plant is pale, short and has no new leaves. The cause of the difference is left open.\"}, \"display\": {\"text\": \"**Two bean plants kept the same way except for light grew very differently in two weeks.** These two plants came from the same batch and stood in identical pots of the same soil. Both were watered the same amount on the same days. One stood on a sunny windowsill; its twin stood in a dark cupboard.\\\\n\\\\nAfter two weeks, the windowsill plant was taller, greener and carrying new leaves. The cupboard plant was pale, short and had added no new leaves. Both plants received the same water and the same soil. What did the windowsill plant use to build its new stem and leaves?\"}, \"id\": \"shared-node-8db81c2aad956244b743\", \"kind\": \"paragraph\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"orient-b1\"}, {\"accessibility\": {\"description\": \"A list of what a plant relies on and how each reaches it: water taken in by the roots and carried up the stem to the leaves; carbon dioxide taken in from the air through the leaves; light captured by the leaves. Soil supplies only water and minerals, never food.\"}, \"display\": {\"items\": [\"Water is taken in by the roots from the soil and carried up the stem to the leaves.\", \"Carbon dioxide is taken in from the air through the leaves.\", \"Light is captured by the leaves.\", \"Soil supplies only water and minerals; it never supplies food.\"], \"ordered\": false}, \"id\": \"shared-node-6582509011cdc33ef8b1\", \"kind\": \"list\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"orient-b2\"}, {\"id\": \"shared-task-anchor-7cb468d182fda7b2e968\", \"kind\": \"task_anchor\", \"role\": null, \"task_spec_id\": \"task-orient-b2\", \"teaching_block_id\": \"orient-b2\"}], \"previous_plan\": {\"avoid_repeating\": [\"No statement of what the leaves do with the three inputs \\\\u2014 the definition belongs to the next section.\", \"No explanation of why the cupboard plant failed to grow.\"], \"blocks\": [{\"brief\": \"Open on the anchor pair: two bean plants from the same batch in identical pots of the same soil, watered the same amount on the same days. One stands on a sunny windowsill, its twin in a dark cupboard. After two weeks the windowsill plant is taller, greener and carrying new leaves; the cupboard plant is pale, short and has added no new leaves. Set out only what was held the same and what was observed, and leave the cause open: state that both plants received the same water and the same soil, and ask what the windowsill plant used to build its new stem and leaves. Do not say that light is the answer, do not explain what a leaf does with anything, and do not call either account of the difference correct or incorrect.\", \"departure_reason\": null, \"evidence\": \"The slot asks for a concrete situation to hold, and the anchor pair is that situation; describing the two plants and their divergence without the cause gives the learner something the later mechanism has to resolve.\", \"evidence_refs\": [\"anchor.anchor-1\", \"slot.orient.purpose\", \"prior-7\"], \"id\": \"orient-b1\", \"intent\": \"orient\", \"learner_action\": null, \"position\": 0, \"source_question_ids\": [], \"sourcebook_needs\": [], \"sourcebook_refs\": [], \"stimulus_dependencies\": [], \"task_mode\": \"none\"}, {\"brief\": \"Recall the three things a plant relies on and how each reaches it: water is taken in by the roots from the soil and carried up the stem to the leaves; carbon dioxide is taken in from the air through the leaves; light is captured by the leaves. Also recall that the soil supplies only water and minerals, never food. Keep this to what learners already know, and stop before saying what the leaves do with the water and the carbon dioxide.\", \"departure_reason\": null, \"evidence\": \"The combining step later in the lesson is impossible to follow unless the learner has the three inputs and their routes live in memory, and this recall is brief and diagnostic rather than new teaching.\", \"evidence_refs\": [\"prior-9\", \"prior-10\", \"prior-6\", \"prior-4\", \"slot.orient.purpose\"], \"id\": \"orient-b2\", \"intent\": \"activate-prior-knowledge\", \"learner_action\": {\"action\": \"match-pairs\", \"difficulty\": \"guided\", \"expected_evidence\": \"water paired with the roots and stem, carbon dioxide paired with the leaves and the air, light paired with the leaves\", \"purpose\": \"retrieve the route of each input before the inputs are combined in the leaves\", \"target\": \"each thing the plant relies on \\\\u2014 water, carbon dioxide, light \\\\u2014 with how it reaches or is captured by the plant\"}, \"position\": 1, \"source_question_ids\": [], \"sourcebook_needs\": [], \"sourcebook_refs\": [], \"stimulus_dependencies\": [], \"task_mode\": \"formative\"}], \"bridge_from_previous\": null, \"display_title\": \"Two bean plants, one difference\", \"entry_state\": [\"Learners know a plant has roots, stems and leaves and that a plant makes its own food rather than taking food from the soil.\", \"Learners know soil supplies water and minerals, and that light is needed for a plant to thrive, but they have not combined these into an account of how food is made.\"], \"exit_state\": [\"Learners hold the bean-plant pair and its unexplained difference in growth.\", \"Learners can say where water, carbon dioxide and light each enter or are captured by a plant.\"], \"must_establish\": [\"The anchor observation: two bean plants in identical pots of the same soil, watered the same amount on the same days, one on a sunny windowsill and one in a dark cupboard; after two weeks only the windowsill plant is taller, greener and carrying new leaves.\", \"That water is taken in by the roots and carried up the stem to the leaves, carbon dioxide is taken in from the air through the leaves, and light is captured by the leaves.\"], \"slot_id\": \"orient\", \"specific_purpose\": \"Open on the anchor pair and get the three inputs into play as routes learners already know.\", \"transition\": null}}'}], 'model': 'deepseek-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 16000, 'stream': False}, 'extra_json': {'thinking': {'type': 'disabled'}}}"}
